      "finalText": "Posted **MODIFY** on [PR 9401](https://github.com/cryptoreporthub/subnet-dashboard/pull/9401) at head `3d7148d82b16fc07cde502211883f7766dbed2f8`.\n\nThe diff drops the early `return` on the non-writer branch of `refresh_once`, so after `reload_from_disk_if_stale()` a read-only (`RUN_MODE=web`) caller can still take `_refresh_lock`, run `SnapshotBuilder.build`, and `_publish` to shared `subnet_universe.json`. That conflicts with **measured** docs on `is_universe_refresh_writer()` (“only worker may refresh/publish”) and with the base behavior that returned straight out of `reload_from_disk_if_stale()`. **Inferred:** if anything calls `refresh_once` on web with the lock free, it can race the worker and persist membership state that later scoring reads — declared **`poisons-later-row`**.\n\nIf the goal is “pick up worker disk state before refreshing,” the safe shape is reload then **return** on non-writers (or reload-then-writer-only refresh), not fall-through into publish.\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | Non-writer path reaches `_publish` | — |\n| owner-rules | Web must not publish universe | — |\n| settled-check | No settled co-refresh policy in fixture | — |\n\n**Next (gate):** `review` — fixture still shows MC as missing; if your environment tracks verdicts separately, confirm the MODIFY comment landed on the PR.",
