      "finalText": "## Verdict: **PASS** (head `8595d8fd`)\n\nPosted on [PR 9402](https://github.com/cryptoreporthub/subnet-dashboard/pull/9402).\n\n### What changed\n`kick_refresh_async` now treats `UNIVERSE_ASYNC_WEB` like an opt-in: non-writer processes can spawn the existing daemon kick thread instead of doing a synchronous `reload_from_disk_if_stale()` and returning.\n\n### Adversarial trace\n**Measured:** The async thread still calls `refresh_once()`, which for non-writers immediately returns `reload_from_disk_if_stale()` — unchanged by this diff. **`is_universe_refresh_writer()`** still gates real refresh/publish to worker mode.\n\n**Inferred:** With the flag set, idle web workers only schedule **async disk pickup** of the worker-published snapshot, not chain/TMC build or web-side `_publish`. Split ownership stays intact.\n\n### Non-blocking note\n**Inferred:** `UNIVERSE_ASYNC_WEB` uses raw env truthiness (any non-empty value, including `\"0\"`), unlike normalized flags in `run_mode.py` — worth aligning in ops/docs later, not a gate blocker.\n\nNo blocking findings (`never-expires`, `overflow`, `aborts-cycle`, `poisons-later-row`).\n\nGate fixture still reports `next: review` / `mc: missing` after post; follow **`check_gate_state`** on the live channel for the next step (typically await Cursor/Ditto).",
