            "body": "## Summary\n\nHead `9914127c` widens `SubnetUniverseProvider.ensure_refresh_loop()` so the background thread may start when `inline_worker_expected()` is true even if `is_universe_refresh_writer()` is false (typical **web** VM with `INLINE_WORKER` and a sibling worker).\n\n## Adversarial trace (real entry points)\n\n**Measured:** `ensure_refresh_loop` → `_refresh_loop` → `refresh_once()`.\n\n**Measured:** `refresh_once()` still returns early to `reload_from_disk_if_stale()` when `not is_universe_refresh_writer()` — web does **not** publish; it only reloads the worker-written persist file. That preserves the writer/reader split in `is_universe_refresh_writer()` (worker via `RUN_MODE=worker`).\n\n**Measured:** `ensure_background_refresh()` at head still does:\n- writer → `ensure_refresh_loop()` + `kick_refresh_async()`\n- non-writer → **only** `ensure_universe_reader()` (one-shot `reload_from_disk_if_stale()`)\n\n**Inferred:** For `INLINE_WORKER` on web, `is_universe_refresh_writer()` is false, so boot via `ensure_background_refresh()` never reaches the new branch in `ensure_refresh_loop()` unless some other caller invokes it (not present in this PR’s single-file diff or the session fixture tree).\n\n**Inferred:** Without a periodic reload loop, web can keep serving in-memory `_snapshot` while the sibling worker updates `subnet_universe.json` on disk (`get_snapshot()` returns memory without reloading).\n\n## Findings\n\n| Sev | Finding | Label |\n|-----|---------|-------|\n| P2 | PR title/ intent (“start refresh loop when INLINE_WORKER is enabled”) is not achieved through the documented boot helper `ensure_background_refresh()`; the changed method appears unreachable on the inline-web path unless wired separately. | **measured** (call graph in `internal/subnet_universe.py`) |\n| P3 | `except Exception` around `inline_worker_expected` import matches local style but masks import failures; on failure behavior reverts to writer-only loop (same as base). | **measured** |\n\n## Recommendation\n\nExtend `ensure_background_refresh()` (or the actual lifespan boot path) so when `inline_worker_expected()` and not writer, it calls `get_provider().ensure_refresh_loop()` plus an initial `ensure_universe_reader()` / kick, mirroring the writer branch’s “loop + immediate refresh” shape.\n\nNo new membership/grace/overflow paths; no blocking gate categories triggered once wiring is complete.\n\n## Skills\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | Traced loop → `refresh_once` writer gate; found boot path gap | — |\n| owner-rules | Writer-only publish unchanged; inline web limited to disk reload in loop | — |\n| settled-check | No roadmap/docs in fixture to settle wiring question | — |",
