      "finalText": "## Verdict: **MODIFY** (head `9914127c`)\n\nPosted on [PR 9405](https://github.com/cryptoreporthub/subnet-dashboard/pull/9405).\n\n### What the diff does (**measured**)\n\n`ensure_refresh_loop()` no longer requires `is_universe_refresh_writer()` when `inline_worker_expected()` is true (after the usual CI/test guard). On a non-writer process, the loop still runs `refresh_once()`, which only **reloads from disk** — it does not publish — so worker/web ownership stays intact.\n\n### Why MODIFY (**measured** + **inferred**)\n\n**Measured:** `ensure_background_refresh()` still only calls `ensure_refresh_loop()` for refresh writers; non-writers get a one-shot `ensure_universe_reader()`.\n\n**Inferred:** On an inline-web VM (`INLINE_WORKER` set, `RUN_MODE=web`), this PR’s change is never reached from that boot helper unless something else calls `ensure_refresh_loop()` (not in this one-file diff).\n\n**Inferred:** Without a periodic reload, web can keep serving in-memory `_snapshot` while the sibling worker updates the persist file.\n\n### Ask\n\nWire the inline-web boot path (likely `ensure_background_refresh()` or lifespan) to call `ensure_refresh_loop()` plus an initial disk reload, similar to the writer branch’s loop + kick pattern.\n\nGate still reports `next: review` in the fixture after post; MC verdict was submitted as **MODIFY**.",
