            "body": "## Summary\n\nOne-line change in `_load_initial_snapshot`: treat a persisted dict as usable LKG when **`netuids` or `rows`** is truthy, then `UniverseSnapshot.from_dict(payload)`.\n\n**Measured:** at head `c3547ea`, only `internal/subnet_universe.py` changes; gate `mc` was missing at this SHA.\n\n## What works\n\n**Measured:** `from_dict` already loads `netuids` from `payload.get(\"netuids\") or []` and `rows` from `payload.get(\"rows\")`, so a file with `\"netuids\": []` and non-empty `rows` becomes an in-memory snapshot with empty membership tuple but intact row payloads.\n\n**Measured:** `_load_initial_snapshot` try/except still falls through to `UniverseSnapshot.emergency_registry` on corrupt JSON or `from_dict` failures — no new uncaught abort on startup.\n\n**Inferred:** Adversarial JSON scalars (`1e308`, bool-as-netuid) follow existing `int(n)` coercion in `from_dict`; this diff does not widen that surface.\n\n## Incomplete vs PR title (P2)\n\nThe PR says *accept LKG files with cleared netuids but intact rows*, but two other entry points still require truthy **`netuids` only**:\n\n1. **`reload_from_disk_if_stale`** (web / reader hot-reload): `not payload.get(\"netuids\")` → keep stale in-memory snapshot. **Measured** at lines 682–683 on head; unchanged by this diff.\n2. **`get_lkg_or_emergency`**: `not snap.netuids` → `emergency_registry(reason=\"no_usable_snapshot\")` even if `_snapshot.rows` is non-empty. **Measured** at lines 782–785; unchanged.\n\n**Inferred:** After a process cold-starts with the new gate, `get_snapshot()` / `get_pump_membership_rows()` can expose row-only LKG, while `get_lkg_or_emergency()` and a later disk reload still fail closed on the same shape — split-brain between consumers.\n\n**Suggested follow-up (same predicate as this PR):** `(payload.get(\"netuids\") or payload.get(\"rows\"))` in `reload_from_disk_if_stale`; decide explicitly whether `get_lkg_or_emergency` should treat non-empty `rows` (or non-empty `validity_map`) as usable LKG or document that empty `netuids` remains fail-closed there by design.\n\n## Grace / membership (P3, not blocking)\n\n**Inferred:** For a corrupt persist where `validity_map` keys are not reflected in `netuids`, `_compute_membership` seeds `prior_members` only from `prior.netuids`, so grace state for netuids absent from this cycle’s `candidates` may not carry until they are observed again. That inconsistency exists in the *file*, not introduced by the boolean change; first successful refresh remains the repair path.\n\n**Settled-check:** `snapshot_coverage.load_membership_receipt` documents owner rule that inactive netuids can remain in membership for grace while marked negative — this diff does not alter `_merge_sources` / `_eligible_for_removal`.\n\n## Owner rules\n\n**Measured:** No change to chain-wins removal, 48h grace, shrink blocking, or emergency persist skip. Scope is LKG load eligibility only.\n\n## Verdict rationale\n\nThe startup load fix is minimal and directionally correct, but the stated acceptance criterion is not applied on the reader reload path (and conflicts with `get_lkg_or_emergency`). Align those gates or narrow the PR claim before PASS.",
