          "args": {
            "body": "## Summary\n\nSmall refactor: `_compute_membership` delegates netuid ordering to new `r1b_f2_netuids_c(validity_map)` in `snapshot_coverage.py` instead of inlining `sorted(int(k) for k in validity_map.keys())`.\n\n## Findings\n\n### P2 — Root netuid dropped from `snap.netuids` while it can remain in `validity_map` (**inferred**, trace through `SnapshotBuilder.build` → `_compute_membership` → persist)\n\n**Measured:** At base, netuids are every `validity_map` key as `int`, including `0` (`ROOT_NETUID`). The added helper (per PR diff) is:\n\n```python\ndef r1b_f2_netuids_c(validity_map):\n    return sorted(k for k in (int(x) for x in validity_map) if max(k, 0))\n```\n\nFor integer keys, `if max(k, 0)` keeps only `k > 0`, so netuid `0` is omitted even when `_compute_membership` still writes `\"0\"` into `validity_map` (when `observed_members` is non-empty and root is not dropped).\n\n**Measured:** `load_membership_receipt()` still sets `root_netuid_in_membership` to `0 in snap.netuids` (not `validity_map`). After this change, root can be a member in `validity_map` while the receipt flag is always false.\n\n**Inferred:** `_build_rows(netuids, …)` no longer emits a row for root when it is only carried in `validity_map`, so `/api/subnets` / pump rows diverge from membership validity for root.\n\n**Inferred edge:** If `validity_map` contained only `\"0\"`, netuids becomes `[]` and `SnapshotBuilder` takes the empty-membership branch while `validity_map` is non-empty — inconsistent persisted state on later cycles (`prior.netuids` loses root even if `prior.validity_map` retained it).\n\n### P3 — Helper shape vs existing coverage idiom (**measured**)\n\n`membership_scoring_expected` already documents positive-only membership as `int(n) > 0`. The new helper uses `if max(k, 0)` (equivalent for ints but opaque) and has no docstring tying it to receipt/scoring semantics.\n\n### P3 — Import placement (**measured**)\n\nLazy import of `internal.council.snapshot_coverage` inside `_compute_membership` couples the universe builder to council on every refresh; no circular import observed at module load (**inferred**), but a top-level shared helper in `subnet_universe` or reusing `membership_scoring_expected` on keys would match existing patterns.\n\n## What looks fine\n\n**Measured:** Numeric keys in `validity_map` come from `str(netuid)` in `_compute_membership`; `int(x)` failure modes match the old `int(k)` loop. No float/`1e308` path in this diff.\n\n## Requested follow-up\n\n1. Align root signaling: either keep `0` in `snap.netuids` when present in `validity_map`, or change `root_netuid_in_membership` (and any row export) to read from `validity_map` in the same change set.\n2. Implement `r1b_f2_netuids_c` with the same explicit `> 0` predicate as `membership_scoring_expected`, plus a short docstring.\n3. Add/adjust a unit test for root-in-membership + positive netuid export (fixture repo here has no tests; full repo should cover this).\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | Root filtered out of netuids; empty-netuids edge when only root in map; traced via real `SnapshotBuilder.build` entry | — |\n| owner-rules | Receipt owner comment on inactive/grace netuids still in `snap.netuids`; root membership comment on line 23 | — |\n| settled-check | No in-repo test lock in this fixture; PR title claims key-shape reuse but receipt still uses `snap.netuids` for root | — |",
