            "body": "## Summary\n\nTwo-file refactor: `_compute_membership` stops doing `sorted(int(k) for k in validity_map.keys())` and calls `r1b_f2_netuids_d(validity_map)` in `internal/chain_price/membership.py` instead.\n\n## Measured behavior change\n\n`r1b_f2_netuids_d` is:\n\n```python\nkeys = [int(k) for k in validity_map.keys()]\nreturn sorted(x for x in keys if x)\n```\n\nThe `if x` filter drops **netuid 0** while `validity_map` can still contain a `\"0\"` entry (root stays in the merge loop; `_eligible_for_removal` never removes `ROOT_NETUID`). Base behavior kept every validity_map key in `netuids`, including 0.\n\nThat matches the existing module comment on `ROOT_NETUID` (chain membership lists root; `get_member_netuids` omits it) and mirrors `get_member_netuids`’s `netuid != 0` filter — **inferred** this is the intended delegation, not an accidental off-by-one.\n\n## Findings\n\n### P2 — LKG shrink can block the rollout on persisted netuid 0\n\n**Measured:** `_eligible_for_removal` returns `False` for `ROOT_NETUID`. **Measured:** `_shrink_allowed` requires drop evidence for every netuid in `prior.netuids - build.snapshot.netuids`. **Inferred:** After deploy, any last-known-good snapshot whose `netuids` still include `0` will produce a build without `0` (new helper) with `0 ∉ dropped`; refresh logs “Unsafe shrink blocked” and `_hold_prior` keeps the old list forever, so the delegated ordering/exclusion never takes effect on those nodes until persistence is repaired or shrink rules treat root specially.\n\n### P3 — Snapshot internal consistency\n\n**Inferred:** On fresh builds (no prior 0), `validity_map` may track `\"0\"` while `netuids` and `_build_rows` omit root, so `universe_snapshot_feed_meta` compares `len(snap.netuids)` to counts over `validity_map` values with an extra root entry. Low severity if root is intentionally non-row, but worth a one-line doc on `r1b_f2_netuids_d` tying it to `get_member_netuids` / `ROOT_NETUID`.\n\n### P4 — Hygiene\n\nLazy import inside `_compute_membership` on every membership resolve; one-line semicolon helper without docstring and opaque name `r1b_f2_netuids_d` vs documented neighbors in the same module.\n\n## Adversarial extremes (same as base for inputs)\n\nKeys come from `str(netuid)` in `_compute_membership` — **measured**. Non-integer keys still raise on `int(k)` — **inferred**, not new. No new float/`inf` paths in this diff.\n\n## Recommendation\n\nLand the delegation after addressing shrink/migration for netuid 0 (explicit root shrink allowance, one-time persist normalization, or document operator step) and add a short docstring on the helper.\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | Traced `_compute_membership` → `SnapshotBuilder.build` → `refresh_once` / `_shrink_allowed`; compared helper filter to base sort | — |\n| owner-rules | Small scoped change; aligns universe list with chain membership omit-root pattern already commented at `ROOT_NETUID` | — |\n| settled-check | `ROOT_NETUID` comment + `#1395 Step 2` module context cover omit-root membership semantics | — |",
