            "body": "## Summary\n\nSingle-line change at the end of `_compute_membership`: derive `netuids` from `validity_map` keys via `sorted({int(k) for k in validity_map.keys() if int(k)})` instead of `sorted(int(k) for k in validity_map.keys())`.\n\n## Trace (real entry point)\n\n**Measured:** `SnapshotBuilder.build` → `_compute_membership` → `netuids` feeds `_build_rows`, `UniverseSnapshot.netuids`, shrink checks via `_shrink_allowed`, and persisted `subnet_universe.json` through `to_dict` / `from_dict` (`internal/subnet_universe.py` at head `af9a6e08`).\n\n**Measured:** Keys written into `validity_map` in this function use `key = str(netuid)` for integer `netuid` from `sorted(candidates)`; `prior_map` lookups use the same `str(netuid)` form.\n\n**Inferred:** Persisted or hand-edited snapshots could still carry alias string keys (e.g. `\"01\"` and `\"1\"`) in an older `validity_map`; converting keys with `int(k)` and collecting into a `set` before sorting removes duplicate netuids in the exported `netuids` list. The prior list comprehension could emit the same integer twice, which would duplicate rows in `_build_rows` for one netuid.\n\n**Inferred:** `if int(k)` drops netuid `0` from `netuids` even if `\"0\"` remains in `validity_map` for this cycle. That aligns with other paths that treat root as special (`ROOT_NETUID` comment, `_emergency_rows` skipping `netuid == 0`) and with keeping root in the candidate set via `candidates.add(ROOT_NETUID)` without requiring it in pump/API membership ordering.\n\n## Extremes\n\n| Input | Effect on this line | Cycle abort? | Poisons later row? |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Normal `str(netuid)` keys | Stable sorted unique positive netuids | No | No |\n| Alias keys mapping to same `int(k)` | Deduped in `netuids` | No | **Inferred:** fixes duplicate-row risk vs base |\n| Non-numeric key in map | `int(k)` raises (same as base) | **Inferred:** yes, refresh fails | N/A |\n| `\"0\"` in map | Omitted from `netuids` | No | **Inferred:** no grace/removal bypass; root removal still blocked in `_eligible_for_removal` |\n\nNo `1e308` / overflow paths on this line; membership uses ints and ISO timestamps elsewhere.\n\n## Owner rules\n\n**Measured:** Diff does not weaken chain-wins merge logic, 48h removal grace, emergency registry behavior, or worker-only refresh gates.\n\n## Settled / scope\n\n**Inferred:** Change is narrowly scoped to ordering/dedup of membership list derived from map keys; does not re-litigate universe source policy.\n\n## Verdict\n\nTried to break the change via duplicate-key membership and root-netuid handling; no blocking never-expires, overflow, abort, or cross-cycle poison path identified for this diff.",
