            "body": "## Summary\n\n**Measured:** Head `e4e74d5ea023a09e38b1efa26fbf2327ae5ce439` changes only `pytest.ini` and `tests/test_subnet_universe.py`. Gate reports `suite: clean`, no prior MC verdict at this SHA, and no production modules in the diff.\n\n## Findings\n\n### P2 — `pytest.ini` deselect is repo-wide, not shard-scoped (**measured** + **inferred**)\n\n**Measured:** `pytest.ini` adds `addopts = --deselect tests/test_subnet_universe.py::test_t1_empty_state_emergency_registry`.\n\n**Inferred:** Pytest applies `[pytest] addopts` to every invocation (local dev, full suite, and each shard). The PR title says universe tests should run on **every shard**; parking T1 deselect in `pytest.ini` also drops `test_t1_empty_state_emergency_registry` everywhere else.\n\n**Measured:** `test_t1` still calls production entry points `SubnetUniverseProvider.get_snapshot()`, `get_lkg_or_emergency()`, and `SnapshotBuilder.build(None)` (cold `emergency_registry` plus a full `MAX_NETUIDS`-width build). It is excluded by config, not removed. **Inferred:** non-shard CI and local runs lose that regression unless something else covers the same paths.\n\n**Ask:** Move the deselect to the sharded workflow command (or a shard-only marker/env) so T1 keeps running outside shards.\n\n### P3 — `test_t9` skipped on all runs for shard timing (**measured**)\n\n**Measured:** `@pytest.mark.skip(reason=\"shard timing\")` on `test_t9_chain_unregistered_beats_tmc_listing`.\n\n**Measured:** The test docstring references the owner rule (2026-10-25) that chain unregistered beats TMC listing while grace applies.\n\n**Inferred:** Skipping is global, not shard-conditional, so CI never exercises T9’s assertions. **Measured:** Related owner-rule scenarios remain in `test_sn7_off_chain_but_tmc_listed_leaves_expected_at_127_and_keeps_its_row` and `test_chain_unregistered_tmc_listed_row_leaves_after_grace_and_stays_gone`, so coverage is partial, not zero.\n\n**Ask:** Fix timing/deadline sensitivity or run T9 in a non-sharded job instead of a permanent skip.\n\n## Adversarial runtime review\n\n**Measured:** No changes to `internal/subnet_universe.py` or other runtime code in this PR’s file list.\n\n**Inferred:** No new acceptance path for extreme floats, non-expiring rows, or cross-cycle poison from this diff alone.\n\n## Direction\n\nEnabling the universe module on every shard is reasonable; narrow T1 deselect to shard runs and replace T9’s blanket skip with a targeted flake fix or job split.",
