            "body": "## Summary\n\nSingle-file change: adds `_api_key_present()` and, when `probe_complete` is false and a netuid is missing from `probe_map`, sets `probe_val` to `None` if `TMC_API_KEY` is non-empty after strip, else `False` (previously always `None`).\n\n## Findings\n\n### P1 — Incomplete probe + synthetic `False` conflicts with “complete chain read” rule (**inferred**)\n\n`_default_probe_fetch` documents that when registration read does not succeed, nothing is observed and `complete` is false so the universe keeps prior members (**measured** in file at head).\n\nThe new branch assigns `probe_val = False` for every candidate not present in `probe_map` whenever `TMC_API_KEY` is absent, still under `not probe_complete`. That includes the failed-read case `probe_map == {}` (**inferred** from `_default_probe_fetch` return paths).\n\n`_merge_sources` applies the owner “chain wins” negative path whenever `probe_positive is False` and `tmc_positive is not False`, with no check that `probe_complete` was true. The inline comment says that path is for a **complete** chain read that omits the netuid (**measured**).\n\n**Effect (**inferred**)**: a timed-out or failed registration pass can stamp many netuids `negative` with fresh `negative_since`, shrinking membership after grace even though the probe explicitly reported incomplete. That state is persisted in `validity_map` and fed back as `prior_map` on the next cycle — bad state later cycles inherit.\n\n**Blocking**: `poisons-later-row`\n\n### P2 — Title vs signal (**inferred**)\n\nPR title references reading an `api_key` **header**; the gate reads `os.environ.get(\"TMC_API_KEY\")` inside `_compute_membership` (**measured**). If production relies on per-request headers without mirroring into env on the worker, the “key present → treat gaps as unknown” branch never runs (**guess**).\n\n### P3 — Coupling chain-gap semantics to TMC credential (**inferred**)\n\nRegistration probe success does not require TMC API key in the code paths available in this fixture (**inferred**). Using `TMC_API_KEY` as the switch for whether missing probe entries mean “unknown” vs “unregistered” mixes unrelated subsystems and is hard to reason about in incident response.\n\n## What would unblock PASS\n\nKeep gap filling at `None` whenever `not probe_complete`, regardless of API key; if a distinct “no TMC, interpret pagination gaps” mode is intended, gate `False` only on evidence that the chain read itself completed (`probe_complete`) and document the env/header source of truth.\n\n## Skills\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | Traced `probe_val` → `_merge_sources` → `validity_map` / `_eligible_for_removal` on failed `probe_map={}` | — |\n| owner-rules | “Complete chain read” comment vs `False` on incomplete gaps | — |\n| settled-check | No roadmap/docs in fixture; not re-litigating prior PRs | skipped: fixture exposes only `internal/subnet_universe.py` |",
