          "args": {
            "body": "## Summary\n\nPR extracts membership netuid list construction into `r1b_member_netuids_from_map_c` and calls it from `_compute_membership`. **Measured:** base used `sorted(int(k) for k in validity_map.keys())`; head uses `sorted(int(k) for k in validity_map.keys() if int(k))`, which **drops netuid 0** whenever key `\"0\"` is present.\n\n## Findings\n\n### P1 — `validity_map` and `snap.netuids` diverge for root (blocking)\n\n**Measured:** `_compute_membership` still adds `ROOT_NETUID` (0) to `candidates` when `observed_members` is non-empty and can write `validity_map[\"0\"]`. **Measured:** `r1b_member_netuids_from_map_c` excludes falsy `int(k)`, so 0 never appears in `netuids` / persisted `snap.netuids` / `_build_rows` output while the `\"0\"` validity entry may remain.\n\n**Inferred:** `load_membership_receipt` exposes `root_netuid_in_membership: 0 in snap.netuids` — after this change that flag no longer reflects a root validity entry, only list membership. Downstream readers that treat `validity_map` as authoritative for “who is a member” vs `netuids` for “who gets rows” can disagree within one snapshot.\n\n**Label:** poisons-later-row (same refresh writes validity for 0 and omits 0 from the membership list later cycles and APIs consume).\n\n### P2 — Unsafe-shrink hold when prior persisted `0` in `netuids`\n\n**Measured:** `_eligible_for_removal` returns `False` for `ROOT_NETUID`. **Measured:** `_shrink_allowed` requires removal evidence for every netuid in `prior.netuids - build.snapshot.netuids`.\n\n**Inferred:** Deployments whose on-disk snapshot still includes `0` in `netuids` (base behavior) will produce builds without `0`; shrink guard fails, `refresh_once` retains LKG (`Unsafe shrink blocked`), so the intended membership list change may never publish.\n\n**Label:** aborts-cycle (refresh writer cannot commit the new membership list across the migration edge).\n\n### P3 — Helper placement and API\n\n**Inferred:** `score_cache.py` is a TTL scoring cache module; universe membership list policy does not belong there (couples council cache to D5 universe semantics). **Measured:** lazy import inside `_compute_membership` hot path; new helper lacks type hints/docstring and uses opaque `r1b_*` naming.\n\n## Adversarial trace (entry: `SnapshotBuilder.build` → `_compute_membership`)\n\n**Measured:** invalid `validity_map` keys still raise via `int(k)` (unchanged vs base). **Measured:** filter does not address overflow/float keys — not introduced here.\n\n## Owner / settled\n\n**Inferred:** Owner-facing coverage code already filters scoring to `int(n) > 0` but separately tracks `root_netuid_in_membership` on `snap.netuids`, implying root in the list was a deliberate observable; this PR changes that observable without updating `snapshot_coverage` or tests in the touched fixture.\n\n**Settled-check:** No in-repo doc/lock in this fixture for `r1b_member_netuids_from_map_c`; behavior change is not a pure refactor.\n\n## Skills\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | Root can remain in `validity_map` but leave `netuids`; shrink block on dropping persisted 0 | — |\n| owner-rules | D5 shared universe + root membership telemetry | — |\n| settled-check | No settled helper; netuid-0 exclusion is new semantics | — |\n\n## Recommendation\n\nKeep the helper on a universe/membership module (or inline with explicit policy comment), align root handling with `ROOT_NETUID` comment and `root_netuid_in_membership`, add/adjust tests for root-in-map vs netuids list and shrink migration, or restore inclusion of 0 if base behavior was correct.",
