            "body": "## Summary\n\nTwo-file refactor: `_compute_membership` delegates netuid list extraction to `r1b_member_netuids_from_map_d` in `internal/chain_price/membership.py`.\n\n## Findings\n\n### 1. Behavioral change — exclude netuid 0 (P3, **inferred** intentional)\n\n**Base (measured):** `netuids = sorted(int(k) for k in validity_map.keys())` — includes `0` when root is present in `validity_map` (root is added to candidates when `observed_members` is non-empty; **measured** in `_compute_membership`).\n\n**Head (measured):** `r1b_member_netuids_from_map_d` returns `sorted(int(k) for k in validity_map.keys() if int(k))` — drops netuid `0`.\n\n**Consumers (inferred):** `SnapshotBuilder.build` → `_build_rows(netuids, …)` → `/api/subnets` row list; `load_membership_receipt` already filters `int(n) > 0` for scoring and tracks `root_netuid_in_membership: 0 in snap.netuids`. Scoring paths explicitly never score root (**measured** in `membership_scoring_candidate_rows` docstring). Aligns with `get_member_netuids` (“excludes netuid 0”) and module comment on `ROOT_NETUID` (**measured** line 22). Effect: root may remain in `validity_map` but no longer appears in exported `netuids`/`rows`; telemetry `root_netuid_in_membership` flips false in that scenario.\n\nNot a blocking category (no never-expire / overflow / cycle abort / cross-cycle poison). Worth one line in the PR body so operators expect the telemetry shift.\n\n### 2. Adversarial key handling (unchanged)\n\nKeys are normally `str(netuid)` from the membership loop (**measured**). Non-numeric keys in a restored `validity_map` still raise `ValueError` on `int(k)` — same as base. Empty map → `[]` (**inferred**).\n\n### 3. Style (P4)\n\nFunction-local import inside `_compute_membership` (**measured**); module-level import would match most of the file. Non-blocking.\n\n### 4. Tests (P4)\n\nNo unit test in fixture tree for `r1b_member_netuids_from_map_d` (especially `{ \"0\": …, \"1\": … }` → `[1]`). Non-blocking for this small helper.\n\n## Verdict rationale\n\nAttempted to break membership resolution via bad keys (same failure mode as before) and via root omission (consistent with chain membership helper and scoring seams). No blocking findings declared.",
