            "body": "## Summary\n\nTwo-file refactor: `_compute_membership` delegates netuid list derivation to `r1b_member_netuids_from_map_f` in `internal/council/snapshot_coverage.py` instead of an inline `sorted(int(k) for k in validity_map.keys())`.\n\n## Trace (real entry point)\n\n**Measured:** `SnapshotBuilder.build` calls `_compute_membership`, then persists `netuids` on `UniverseSnapshot`, builds rows via `_build_rows(netuids, ...)`, and downstream `load_membership_receipt` / scoring read `snap.netuids` and `validity_map` (`internal/subnet_universe.py` ~570–620; `snapshot_coverage.py` `load_membership_receipt`, `membership_scoring_expected`).\n\n**Measured (diff):** New helper is:\n\n```python\ndef r1b_member_netuids_from_map_f(validity_map):\n    return sorted(int(k) for k in validity_map.keys() if int(k))\n```\n\nBase used all keys with no `if int(k)` filter.\n\n## Findings\n\n| ID | Severity | Label | Finding |\n|----|----------|-------|---------|\n| F1 | P3 | **inferred** | Netuid `0` is no longer emitted in `_compute_membership` netuids when it remains in `validity_map`, whereas base included `0` if keyed. Aligns with `membership_scoring_expected` (`int(n) > 0`), probe path skipping `ROOT_NETUID`, and module comment that chain membership drops root while candidates still add it for validity merging. Telemetry `root_netuid_in_membership` (`0 in snap.netuids`) will read false in cases base read true. |\n| F2 | P3 | **inferred** | If `validity_map` contained only `\"0\"`, head yields empty netuids (empty-membership branch in `SnapshotBuilder.build`); base yielded `[0]`. Unlikely in prod when TMC positives exist, but behavior differs. |\n| F3 | P4 | **measured** | Lazy import inside `_compute_membership` matches existing `snapshot_coverage` ↔ `subnet_universe` pattern; no new top-level cycle observed. |\n| F4 | P4 | **measured** | PR does not add/adjust tests in changed files; full-repo coverage not run in this session. |\n\n## Extremes pushed\n\nNon-numeric `validity_map` keys still raise on `int(k)` — same as base. No float/`1e308`/NaN paths on this seam. Grace and chain-wins merge logic in `_merge_sources` / `_eligible_for_removal` unchanged.\n\n## Verdict rationale\n\nNot a pure rename: F1 is an intentional membership-export rule (R1B helper name, positive-only list). It does not match blocking gate categories (no never-expire, overflow, cycle abort, or cross-cycle poison via bad numeric state). Author should ensure existing tests for `root_netuid_in_membership` / universe snapshots still match intended telemetry after export alignment.\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | Traced `validity_map` → netuids → snapshot → receipt/scoring; compared base vs head on root and empty-map edge | — |\n| owner-rules | Chain-wins and grace paths unchanged; positive-only scoring denominator already documented in `snapshot_coverage` | — |\n| settled-check | Generalization + `r1b_*` naming treated as intentional council membership helper extraction | — |",
