            "body": "## Summary\n\nExtracts ISO parsing from `_eligible_for_removal` into `_parse_negative_since` and adds a small unit test. **Measured** (diff + head reads): logic matches the prior inline `try`/`fromisoformat`/naive→UTC/`except` path; `_eligible_for_removal` still returns `False` on parse failure.\n\n## Entry point (adversarial trace)\n\nProduction shrink gate: `SubnetUniverseProvider.refresh_once` → `_shrink_allowed` → `_eligible_for_removal(netuid, evidence, now)` (`internal/subnet_universe.py`). `evidence.negative_since` comes from `DropEvidence` built during `_compute_membership` / refresh. **Inferred**: unchanged control flow — unparseable timestamps still block removal eligibility, so unsafe shrink remains blocked via `_hold_prior` (same as base).\n\n## Edge values\n\n| Input | Result | vs base |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| missing / falsy `negative_since` | early `False` before parse | **Measured** same |\n| valid naive ISO | UTC-aware `datetime` | **Measured** same; new test locks this |\n| garbage string | `None` → `False` | **Measured** same |\n| aware ISO | `fromisoformat` + no replace | **Inferred** same |\n\n`(now - started).total_seconds() >= STALE_GRACE_SECONDS` unchanged; no new overflow path introduced by the extract.\n\n## Owner / settled\n\n**Inferred**: no change to 48h grace (`STALE_GRACE_SECONDS`), probe gate, or root netuid exclusion. Refactor-only; existing integration tests (`test_chain_unregistered_row_leaves_after_grace_…`, shrink regression) still cover removal timing.\n\n## Nits (non-blocking)\n\n- **Guess**: `_parse_negative_since` is module-private but imported in-test — consistent with other `_` helpers in this test module.\n- Optional follow-up: test an offset-aware ISO string if we want parity documentation; not required for this extract.\n\nNo blocking findings (`never-expires`, `overflow`, `aborts-cycle`, `poisons-later-row`).",
