            "body": "PASS @ 354a4ec473bbfbb64aff7575cd16ea2360488426\n\n## Scope (measured)\nTwo new files: `internal/r1b_perf_08.py` defines `queries_for_refresh(netuid_count, *, batch_size=32)`; `tests/test_r1b_perf_08.py` asserts `queries_for_refresh(64, batch_size=32) == 2`.\n\n## Adversarial trace (inferred unless noted)\n**Real entry points at this head:** the unit test and direct calls to `queries_for_refresh`. **Measured:** fixture tree at head lists no importer of `internal.r1b_perf_08` besides the test — no refresh scheduler, metrics, or cycle loop consumes this yet.\n\nFor `netuid_count > 0` and `batch_size > 0`, the body `(netuid_count + batch_size - 1) // batch_size` is standard integer ceiling division (e.g. 33→2 at batch 32). **Measured:** `netuid_count <= 0` returns `0` before division.\n\nExtremes: Python ints do not overflow to `inf`/`NaN` on the add/divide path. **Inferred:** invalid `batch_size <= 0` would raise `ZeroDivisionError` or wrong counts if a future caller passed config without validation — not exercised in this diff and not on a cycle entry point today.\n\nNo row state, expiry, or cross-cycle persistence — nothing that fits `never-expires`, `overflow`, `aborts-cycle`, or `poisons-later-row` on the shipped surface.\n\n## Non-blocking notes (MODIFY optional, not gate-blocking)\n- **Inferred:** Tests cover one happy path only; `netuid_count=0` and a partial batch (e.g. 33) would lock the contract.\n- **Inferred:** When this is wired to refresh batching, validate `batch_size` at the config/env seam (same pattern as `env_int` + `max(1, …)` elsewhere).\n\n## Skills\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | Traced `queries_for_refresh`; no prod consumer at head; ceiling math OK for positive inputs | — |\n| owner-rules | skipped: skill file not readable via session tools; no membership/scoring/cap logic in diff | — |\n| settled-check | skipped: no roadmap/lock artifacts in fixture repo for this slice | — |",
