      "finalText": "**MODIFY** posted on [PR 9401](https://github.com/cryptoreporthub/subnet-dashboard/pull/9401) at head `3d7148d82b16fc07cde502211883f7766dbed2f8`.\n\n### What changed (measured)\nIn `refresh_once`, when `is_universe_refresh_writer()` is false, the code still calls `reload_from_disk_if_stale()` but no longer returns there. It can continue into the non-blocking `_refresh_lock`, run `_builder.build`, and `_publish` (including disk persist).\n\n### Why MODIFY (not PASS)\n1. **Cross-process coordination (inferred):** `_refresh_lock` is a **thread** lock, per process. On split web/worker, web and worker can both refresh and write `subnet_universe.json` without sharing that mutex. That fits “share refresh work” in direction only, not in safety for a shared persist file.\n2. **Doc drift (measured):** `is_universe_refresh_writer()` and `ensure_universe_reader()` still say web only reloads and never refresh/publish, while non-writers can now reach `_publish` via `refresh_once`.\n3. **Boot path today (measured in available code):** `ensure_background_refresh()` / `kick_refresh_async()` on non-writers still mostly reload-only, so the new path matters once something calls `refresh_once` on web—which the PR title implies.\n\n### Adversarial numerics\nNo new float/grace ingress in this one-line diff; membership merge logic is unchanged.\n\nGate `next` remains `review` in the fixture after posting; Cursor/Ditto/suite steps follow your gate bot’s normal flow.",
