            "body": "## Summary\n\nSingle-line gate in `kick_refresh_async`: when `UNIVERSE_ASYNC_WEB` is set, non-writer processes skip the synchronous `reload_from_disk_if_stale()` early return and instead spawn the existing daemon kick thread.\n\n## Trace (measured / inferred)\n\n**Measured:** On non-writer processes, `refresh_once()` still returns immediately into `reload_from_disk_if_stale()` (`internal/subnet_universe.py` ~712–714). The async thread therefore does **not** run TMC/probe build or `_publish`; it only reloads the worker-persisted snapshot, matching `is_universe_refresh_writer()`’s doc (“web reloads persisted snapshots”).\n\n**Measured:** `ensure_background_refresh()` still calls `ensure_universe_reader()` on non-writers and never reaches `kick_refresh_async()` (~841–847). In this fixture tree the new env flag only affects direct `kick_refresh_async()` callers (not shown here); wiring may live outside the truncated listing.\n\n**Inferred:** With `UNIVERSE_ASYNC_WEB=0` or `false`, `os.environ.get(\"UNIVERSE_ASYNC_WEB\")` is still truthy, enabling the async path—unlike `background_on_web()` / `BACKGROUND_ON_WEB` parsing in `internal/run_mode.py`, which treats explicit off values as disabled.\n\n## Findings\n\n| Sev | Finding | Label |\n|-----|---------|-------|\n| P2 | Parse `UNIVERSE_ASYNC_WEB` with the same explicit off tokens as other web background flags, or document that any non-empty value enables async; otherwise `=0` silently flips behavior. | inferred |\n| P3 | If the goal is async **disk reload** only, consider calling `reload_from_disk_if_stale` inside `_run` for the non-writer branch instead of routing through `refresh_once()` (clearer intent, same effect today). | inferred |\n| — | No numeric membership inputs touched; no new shrink/grace/expiry paths in this hunk. | measured |\n\n## Blocking categories\n\nNone declared (`never-expires`, `overflow`, `aborts-cycle`, `poisons-later-row` not introduced by this diff).\n\n## Skills\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | Traced env gate → kick thread → `refresh_once` → reader reload for non-writers; env string extremes | — |\n| owner-rules | Writer-only publish unchanged at `refresh_once`; web still reader unless worker mode | — |\n| settled-check | skipped: no locks/roadmap artifacts in session fixture | — |",
