      "finalText": "Posted **MODIFY** on PR [9402](https://github.com/cryptoreporthub/subnet-dashboard/pull/9402) at head `8595d8fd288d013e8f2f75b16fb5c3bff29c0356`.\n\n**What the change does (measured):** `UNIVERSE_ASYNC_WEB` lets non-writer processes take the async kick path instead of calling `reload_from_disk_if_stale()` synchronously and returning. The kick thread still calls `refresh_once()`, and for non-writers `refresh_once()` only reloads from disk—it does not build or publish. That matches the existing writer-only publish rule.\n\n**Why MODIFY (inferred):** `os.environ.get(\"UNIVERSE_ASYNC_WEB\")` is truthy for any non-empty value, so `UNIVERSE_ASYNC_WEB=0` or `=false` would still enable async behavior, unlike explicit off handling in `internal/run_mode.py` for other web background flags.\n\n**Blocking:** None of the four blocking categories apply to this hunk.\n\nGate `next` still reads `review` in the fixture session after the post; the verdict comment is on the PR.",
