            "body": "## Summary\n\nSingle hunk in `SubnetUniverseProvider.reload_from_disk_if_stale`: split the old combined guard so a dict payload with **falsy `netuids`** is still loaded when `status` is **`ok` or `degraded`**, instead of keeping stale in-memory LKG.\n\n## Trace (real entry points)\n\n**Measured:** Non-writer paths call `reload_from_disk_if_stale` from `refresh_once`, `kick_refresh_async`, and `ensure_universe_reader` (`ensure_background_refresh` on web). Readers pick up worker `_atomic_persist` writes when `mtime` advances.\n\n**Measured:** `_atomic_persist` skips `emergency_registry` only; worker publishes full `snap.to_dict()` including `netuids`, `status`, `validity_map`, and `rows`.\n\n**Measured:** `SnapshotBuilder` can produce a persisted **`degraded`** snapshot with **`netuids=()`** (e.g. empty membership / refresh-incomplete hold paths). Before this PR, `not payload.get(\"netuids\")` rejected that on reload, so web processes could **ignore a newer on-disk snapshot** and keep an older in-memory universe — split-worker drift.\n\n**Measured:** After reload, `UniverseSnapshot.from_dict` still builds `netuids` only from the `netuids` array (not from `validity_map` keys). Malformed `netuids` types that blow up `int(...)` are caught by the existing `except` and leave LKG unchanged.\n\n**Measured:** `get_lkg_or_emergency` still replaces **`emergency_registry` or empty `netuids`** with `emergency_registry(reason=\"no_usable_snapshot\")` for fail-closed callers; this PR does not weaken that seam.\n\n## Adversarial / edge values\n\n| Input | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| non-dict JSON root | Early return; LKG kept (**measured**) |\n| `netuids: []`, `status` missing / not ok·degraded | Reload skipped (**measured**) |\n| `netuids: []`, `status: \"ok\"\\|\"degraded\"` | Loaded; scoring/pump paths that key off empty membership stay fail-closed or row-driven as before (**inferred** from consumers read) |\n| corrupt `netuids` (e.g. non-int elements) | Exception path; LKG kept (**measured**) |\n\nNo path found where this hunk alone lets a value overflow to `inf`/`NaN`, prevents grace expiry, or aborts a refresh cycle via uncaught numeric edge cases.\n\n## Owner rules\n\n**Measured:** `is_universe_refresh_writer()` restricts publish/refresh to worker (web reload-only). Honoring ok/degraded disk snapshots when `netuids` is empty matches worker-published degraded membership instead of silently retaining stale web LKG — aligned with split Fly worker ownership.\n\n**Inferred (P3, out of diff):** `_load_initial_snapshot` still requires truthy `netuids` on cold start; a first boot against a compact empty-but-degraded file still goes through `emergency_registry` until a stale reload runs. Consider aligning initial load with this guard in a follow-up, not blocking here.\n\n## Settled-check\n\nNo lock/roadmap text in the fixture tree for this guard; the behavioral intent (web must not ignore worker-persisted ok/degraded snapshots) matches the PR title and existing publish/reload split.\n\n## Verdict\n\n**PASS** — fixes real split-process stale-LKG behavior with a narrow, status-gated admission rule; no blocking never-expires / overflow / abort-cycle / poison-later-row finding tied to this change.",
