      "finalText": "**PASS** posted for head `229a31e307a6d172616e1e63b630bb1ab4a42259` on [PR 9403](https://github.com/cryptoreporthub/subnet-dashboard/pull/9403).\n\nThe change fixes split web/worker behavior: `reload_from_disk_if_stale` used to skip any payload with falsy `netuids`, so web could keep stale in-memory LKG while the worker had already persisted a legitimate **`ok`/`degraded`** snapshot with an empty membership list. The new guard only rejects empty `netuids` when `status` is not `ok` or `degraded`.\n\nNo blocking findings (`never-expires`, `overflow`, `aborts-cycle`, `poisons-later-row`). **P3 follow-up (non-blocking):** `_load_initial_snapshot` still requires truthy `netuids` on cold boot; aligning it with this reload rule would close the same gap at process start.\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | Reload entry points; empty `netuids` + ok/degraded vs stale LKG; `from_dict` exception path | — |\n| owner-rules | Web reload-only vs worker publish; `get_lkg_or_emergency` fail-closed | — |\n| settled-check | No settled doc in fixture; matches writer/reload split | — |\n\nGate fixture still reports `next: review` and `mc: missing` after post; in production the recorded MC verdict should advance the gate toward Cursor/Ditto.",
