            "body": "## Summary\n\nThree-line fix in `reload_from_disk_if_stale` on `SubnetUniverseProvider`: split the old combined guard so non-dict payloads still bail early, and treat a persisted payload as reloadable when **either** `netuids` **or** `rows` is present.\n\n## What was wrong (measured)\n\n**Measured:** At base, reload used `if not isinstance(payload, dict) or not payload.get(\"netuids\"): return self._snapshot` — so a worker-published file with populated `rows` but missing/empty `netuids` (mid-migration / row-backed persist) never updated web readers even after mtime advanced.\n\n**Measured:** `ensure_universe_reader()` → `reload_from_disk_if_stale()` is the web/read-only entry (`internal/subnet_universe.py`); writers publish via `_atomic_persist` + `snap.to_dict()`, which always includes both `netuids` and `rows` when the builder succeeds.\n\n## Adversarial trace (inferred)\n\n**Inferred:** After reload, `UniverseSnapshot.from_dict` still builds `netuids` only from the `netuids` key (`payload.get(\"netuids\") or []`), not from `rows` or `validity_map`. A rows-only file therefore yields `snap.netuids == ()` while `snap.rows` may be populated.\n\n**Inferred:** Downstream, `load_membership_receipt()` pins `expected_netuids` from `snap.netuids` (`internal/council/snapshot_coverage.py`), so scoring admission fail-closes when netuids are empty; `get_pump_membership_rows()` can still serve row payloads from `snap.rows`. That is degraded/consistency during a deliberate migration window, not unbounded grace or silent shrink approval on the writer path (writers still run `_shrink_allowed` / `_compute_membership` on refresh).\n\n**Inferred:** `_load_initial_snapshot()` still requires `payload.get(\"netuids\")` on cold start — unchanged by this PR. Follow-up parity optional; not introduced here.\n\n## Extremes\n\nNo new float/parse surface in the diff. Malformed JSON or `from_dict` failures remain in the existing `except` path and retain prior in-memory LKG.\n\n## Owner rules\n\nRow-backed shared universe (D5) and fail-closed scoring when membership receipt is incomplete/stale remain intact; this change only widens **when** readers accept a disk publish, aligned with `to_dict()` already persisting `rows`.\n\n## Settled-check\n\nNo re-litigation of chain-wins / 48h grace logic; diff does not touch `_merge_sources`, `_eligible_for_removal`, or refresh builder.\n\n## Verdict\n\nPASS — targeted reload fix for split web/worker deploy; no blocking never-expires / overflow / abort-cycle / poison-later-row finding in the changed path.",
