      "sessionId": "ses_b941afd2881c625a4cce711c",
      "finalText": "Posted **PASS** on head `92f5a7759d754a12262f45ac839e0d7167d4a427` for PR [#9404](https://github.com/cryptoreporthub/subnet-dashboard/pull/9404).\n\n**Change:** `reload_from_disk_if_stale` no longer requires `netuids` alone. It reloads when the on-disk JSON is a dict and at least one of `netuids` or `rows` is present, so web readers can pick up row-backed worker publishes during a `netuids` migration.\n\n**Review:** The old guard blocked reload whenever `netuids` was missing or empty even if `rows` was populated, leaving split web processes on stale LKG after mtime moved. **Measured:** `from_dict` still builds membership IDs only from the `netuids` key, so rows-only files can yield empty `snap.netuids` while rows update—scoring receipts fail closed on empty expected netuids; pump rows can still come from `snap.rows`. No new overflow, cycle-abort, unbounded grace, or poisoned-state paths in this diff. `_load_initial_snapshot` still requires `netuids` on cold start (unchanged; optional follow-up).\n\n**Blocking:** none declared.\n\nGate `next` still reads `review` in this fixture session after the post; formal MC comment is on the PR with the required Skills table.",
