            "body": "## Summary\n\nHead `9914127c` relaxes `SubnetUniverseProvider.ensure_refresh_loop()` so the background thread may start when `inline_worker_expected()` is true, not only when `is_universe_refresh_writer()` is true. CI/test early exit is unchanged.\n\n## Measured\n\n- Diff touches only `ensure_refresh_loop` in `internal/subnet_universe.py` (+8/−1).\n- **`is_universe_refresh_writer()`** (**measured**, head): returns `is_worker_mode()` outside CI/test — web stays a non-writer.\n- **`refresh_once()`** (**measured**): non-writers call `reload_from_disk_if_stale()` only; they never publish.\n- **`ensure_background_refresh()`** (**measured**, head): still calls `provider.ensure_refresh_loop()` **only** when `is_universe_refresh_writer()`; the `else` branch is `ensure_universe_reader()` (one-shot disk reload, no loop).\n- In this head snapshot, **`ensure_refresh_loop` is referenced only from `ensure_background_refresh`** within the available tree.\n\n## Inferred\n\n- For Fly v1 **web** (`RUN_MODE=web`, `INLINE_WORKER=on`), the intended fix is likely periodic disk reload while a sibling worker publishes to shared storage — the loop body would only poll disk on web, which is consistent with the writer gate in `refresh_once()`.\n- With the current boot seam unchanged, that web process **still never calls** `ensure_refresh_loop()` through `ensure_background_refresh()`, so the new `inline_worker_expected()` branch is **dead on the primary entry path** unless some other module (not present in this review snapshot) invokes `ensure_refresh_loop()` directly.\n\n## Findings\n\n| ID | Sev | Label | Finding |\n|----|-----|-------|---------|\n| F1 | P2 | **inferred** | **`ensure_background_refresh()` not updated** — loop start for `INLINE_WORKER` web hosts requires either extending `ensure_background_refresh()` (e.g. start loop + reader path when `inline_worker_expected()` and not writer) or a documented direct caller; as shipped, behavior for inline web boot may be unchanged. |\n| F2 | P3 | **inferred** | Broad `except Exception` around the import/check falls back to writer-only — safe degradation, but a broken `run_mode` import silently drops the new behavior (same pattern as `is_universe_refresh_writer()`). |\n\nNo change in membership math, grace expiry, or refresh publish logic in this diff — **not** in the never-expires / overflow / abort-cycle / poison-row classes.\n\n## Recommendation\n\nExtend the real boot entry (`ensure_background_refresh` or the lifespan hook that owns it) so `INLINE_WORKER` web machines actually invoke `ensure_refresh_loop()`, and add/adjust a test that boots with `RUN_MODE=web` + `INLINE_WORKER=on` and asserts the loop thread starts without calling `refresh_once` publish paths.\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | Traced loop start → `ensure_background_refresh` → writer gate; traced loop body → `refresh_once` writer gate | — |\n| owner-rules | Worker-only publish unchanged; web read path unchanged in `ensure_background_refresh` | — |\n| settled-check | No roadmap/docs in fixture for INLINE_WORKER loop wiring | skipped: no settled doc in snapshot |",
