            "body": "## Summary\n\nOne-line change widens `_load_initial_snapshot` so persisted JSON with falsy `netuids` but non-empty `rows` calls `UniverseSnapshot.from_dict` instead of falling through to `emergency_registry`. That matches the PR title, but the same acceptance predicate is not applied on the web reader reload path, and `from_dict` still materializes an empty `netuids` tuple when the list is cleared—downstream membership and LKG helpers then behave as if there is no universe.\n\n## Findings\n\n### P1 — `reload_from_disk_if_stale` still requires truthy `netuids` (**measured**)\n\n`_load_initial_snapshot` (head) uses `(payload.get(\"netuids\") or payload.get(\"rows\"))`. `reload_from_disk_if_stale` still has `not payload.get(\"netuids\")` → early return (lines ~676–679 at head). On split web/worker deployments, `ensure_universe_reader()` only reloads via this method. A worker-published file in the shape this PR targets is accepted on cold start but **ignored** on stale reload, so web processes can keep an older in-memory snapshot while disk holds rows-only LKG.\n\n### P1 — Cleared `netuids` + intact `rows` → empty membership in memory (**measured** + **inferred**)\n\n`UniverseSnapshot.from_dict` sets `netuids = tuple(sorted(int(n) for n in payload.get(\"netuids\") or []))` and loads `rows` separately; it does **not** backfill `netuids` from row `netuid` fields or `validity_map` keys.\n\nConsumers (**measured** in `internal/subnet_universe.py`):\n- `get_netuids()` → `list(self._snapshot.netuids)` → `[]`\n- `get_lkg_or_emergency()` → `not snap.netuids` forces `emergency_registry(reason=\"no_usable_snapshot\")` even when `snap.rows` is populated\n- `get_pump_membership_rows()` would still return rows (**measured**), so pump vs membership APIs diverge on the same snapshot\n\n`SnapshotBuilder.build` sets `prior_members = set(prior.netuids)` (**measured**). `_compute_membership` iterates `candidates = prior_members | observed_members` (**measured**). Netuids present only in `validity_map` / row payload but absent from `prior.netuids` are not in `candidates` (**inferred** from loop structure), so the next refresh can drop membership that the on-disk file still encodes—**poisons-later-row**.\n\n### P2 — Log line misleading after load (**measured**)\n\nLog still says `loaded LKG: %d netuids` with `len(snap.netuids)`; for cleared-netuids files this reads `0` while rows may be non-empty.\n\n## Recommendation\n\nAlign `reload_from_disk_if_stale` with the same `(netuids or rows)` gate; reconcile `netuids` in `from_dict` (from rows and/or `validity_map`) when the list is empty; consider `get_lkg_or_emergency` treating row-backed snapshots as usable when rows or validity_map imply membership. Add a regression test for persisted `{netuids: [], rows: [...]}` on both initial load and disk reload.\n\nNo float/overflow path touched in this diff.",
