      "finalText": "Posted **MODIFY** on PR 9406 at head `c3547ea757c657fc0d34145feb1745b9a51a0773` (blocking: **poisons-later-row**).\n\nThe diff only relaxes the gate in `_load_initial_snapshot` so a dict with falsy `netuids` but non-empty `rows` reaches `UniverseSnapshot.from_dict`. That matches the title, but the fix is incomplete:\n\n1. **`reload_from_disk_if_stale` (measured)** — Still requires truthy `payload.get(\"netuids\")`. Web readers (`ensure_universe_reader`) will not pick up the same on-disk shape after a worker publish, while cold start would.\n\n2. **`from_dict` + consumers (measured / inferred)** — Cleared `netuids` still yields `snap.netuids == ()` while `rows` may be full. `get_lkg_or_emergency()` treats `not snap.netuids` as unusable and returns emergency; `get_netuids()` is empty; `get_pump_membership_rows()` can still return rows — split behavior on one snapshot. On refresh, `prior_members = set(prior.netuids)` can drop membership that only lives in `validity_map`/rows (**poisons-later-row**).\n\nSuggested follow-up: mirror the `(netuids or rows)` check on reload, reconcile `netuids` when the list is empty (from rows and/or `validity_map`), and add tests for initial load and disk reload.\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | Load vs reload paths; empty `netuids` with rows through `build` / `_compute_membership` | — |\n| owner-rules | Receipt/scoring uses `snap.netuids`; rows-only load breaks membership honesty | — |\n| settled-check | No settled exception for this partial gate in fixture scope | — |",
