lready centralized in `is_tradable_subnet`. Prefer an explicit named helper (e.g. `membership_netuids_from_validity_map`) using `int(k) > 0` or shared tradable predicate.\n\n4. **Telemetry (P4)**  \n   `load_membership_receipt` exposes `root_netuid_in_membership: 0 in snap.netuids`; after this change that flag goes false even when Root remains in `validity_map` — observability shift, not necessarily wrong if Root should leave `netuids`.\n\n## Extremes (same as base unless noted)\n\n- Non-numeric `validity_map` keys: `int(x)` still raises → refresh path can fail inside `_compute_membership` (**aborts-cycle**, pre-existing).\n- Large / negative ints: still admitted if present as keys; no new overflow path in this diff.\n\n## Ask\n\n- Exempt `ROOT_NETUID` in `_shrink_allowed`, **or** stop retaining Root in `validity_map` when excluding from `netuids`, **or** migrate persisted snapshots — plus a test covering prior `{0, …}` → refresh publishes without shrink block.\n\nNo execution or pytest in this review.",
