            "body": "## Summary\n\nThis PR replaces `_compute_membership`'s local `sorted(int(k) for k in validity_map.keys())` with `r1b_f2_netuids_c(validity_map)` in `internal/council/snapshot_coverage.py`.\n\n## Findings\n\n### P1 — Root netuid dropped from membership export (blocking)\n\n**measured:** Base `_compute_membership` builds `netuids` from every `validity_map` key (`sorted(int(k) for k in validity_map.keys())`). The new helper is:\n\n```python\ndef r1b_f2_netuids_c(validity_map):\n    return sorted(k for k in (int(x) for x in validity_map) if max(k, 0))\n```\n\n**measured:** `if max(k, 0)` is falsy for `k <= 0`, so netuid **0** never appears in `netuids` even when `validity_map[\"0\"]` is written (ROOT is still added to `candidates` when `observed_members` is non-empty, and `_eligible_for_removal` never removes root).\n\n**inferred:** `_build_rows` iterates `netuids` only, so root stops getting a row while `validity_map` can still hold a positive entry for `\"0\"`. Persisted snapshots then disagree with themselves (`validity_map` vs `netuids`/`rows`).\n\n**inferred:** `load_membership_receipt` exposes `root_netuid_in_membership: 0 in snap.netuids` (**measured** in base `snapshot_coverage.py`). After this change, that flag goes false whenever root would previously have been listed, even though universe logic still treats root as special.\n\n**inferred:** Later refresh cycles seed `prior_members` from `prior.netuids` (**measured** in `SnapshotBuilder.build`). Omitting 0 from `netuids` drops root from `prior_members` unless `observed_members` is non-empty again, so LKG can **lose root from the exported membership list** while grace/validity state still references it — bad state read back on the next cycle (`poisons-later-row`).\n\n**Fix direction:** If the goal is to match coverage's positive-netuid scoring shape, do that at the coverage boundary (`membership_scoring_expected` already uses `int(n) > 0`) without stripping root from the shared universe export, **or** filter with the same explicit predicate used elsewhere (`int(k) > 0`) only if product confirms root must leave `snap.netuids`, and update root telemetry/tests accordingly. Prefer a named helper (e.g. `membership_export_netuids`) with a docstring instead of `r1b_f2_netuids_c`.\n\n### P3 — Opaque helper / inconsistent idiom\n\n**measured:** Elsewhere in `snapshot_coverage`, positive membership IDs use `int(n) > 0` (e.g. `load_membership_receipt`, `membership_scoring_expected`). `if max(k, 0)` is equivalent for integers but is harder to audit and does not match local style.\n\n**measured:** No tests or call-site comments ship with the rename; fixture diff only touches two files.\n\n## Extremes (adversarial-review)\n\n**measured:** `validity_map` keys in `_compute_membership` are always `str(netuid)` from the candidate loop — corrupt non-numeric keys would fail `int()` on base and head alike (**inferred:** aborts that refresh call, not new to this PR).\n\n**inferred:** No float overflow path in this change (not applicable).\n\n## Gate\n\nMC review only; no PASS while root export desync remains.",
