      "sessionId": "ses_1f9099402075a586bc411779",
      "finalText": "## Verdict: **MODIFY** (posted on PR 9409 @ `3a543a09`)\n\nThe new helper `r1b_f2_netuids_c` does not behave like the old line it replaces.\n\n**Measured:** Base code sets `netuids = sorted(int(k) for k in validity_map.keys())`, so every validity entry (including netuid **0**) is exported. The new filter `if max(k, 0)` drops `k <= 0`, so root can remain in `validity_map` but disappear from `netuids`, rows, and `root_netuid_in_membership` (`0 in snap.netuids` in `load_membership_receipt`).\n\n**Inferred (blocking — `poisons-later-row`):** Later refreshes take `prior_members` from `prior.netuids`, so root can fall out of the exported membership list while universe logic still treats root as special—persisted LKG no longer matches how the next cycle seeds membership.\n\n**P3:** The `max(k, 0)` idiom does not match the explicit `int(n) > 0` pattern used elsewhere in `snapshot_coverage`, and the `r1b_f2_*` name ships without tests or a docstring.\n\n**Suggested direction:** Keep root on the shared universe export unless product explicitly wants it removed; if positive-only filtering is only for scoring, keep that at `membership_scoring_expected` / coverage boundaries. Use a clearly named, documented helper and align the predicate with existing style.\n\nGate `next` still reads `review` in the fixture after post; MC verdict was accepted as MODIFY.",
