            "body": "## Summary\n\nHead `bca36052f6be11c67b52c733747a7373cf2ff74a` delegates universe netuid ordering from `_compute_membership` to new `r1b_f2_netuids_d(validity_map)` in `internal/chain_price/membership.py`.\n\n## Findings\n\n### P1 — Silent drop of netuid 0 vs unsafe-shrink gate (**inferred**)\n\n**Base behavior (measured from base `subnet_universe.py`):**\n```python\nnetuids = sorted(int(k) for k in validity_map.keys())\n```\nEvery validity_map key, including `\"0\"` (`ROOT_NETUID`), becomes part of `netuids` when present.\n\n**Head behavior (measured from head `membership.py`):**\n```python\ndef r1b_f2_netuids_d(validity_map):\n    keys = [int(k) for k in validity_map.keys()]; return sorted(x for x in keys if x)\n```\nThe `if x` filter removes netuid **0** while `validity_map` can still retain `\"0\"` (`ROOT_NETUID` is never eligible for removal in `_eligible_for_removal`).\n\n**Consumer trace (inferred):** `SnapshotBuilder.build` → `refresh_once` → `_shrink_allowed(prior, build)` compares `prior.netuids` to `build.snapshot.netuids`. For any netuid in `set(prior.netuids) - set(build.netuids)`, shrink requires `build.dropped[netuid]` with `_eligible_for_removal` true. Netuid 0 is excluded from `build.snapshot.netuids` by the helper but is **not** placed in `dropped` with eligible evidence (`_eligible_for_removal` returns False for `ROOT_NETUID`). Shrink is therefore blocked and the refresh retains LKG via `_hold_prior`.\n\n**Operational effect (inferred):** Persisted snapshots that already list `0` in `netuids` (expected today when root is in `validity_map`; telemetry explicitly tracks `root_netuid_in_membership`: `0 in snap.netuids` in `snapshot_coverage.py`) will hit the unsafe-shrink path on every refresh after this change, preventing publication of otherwise-valid membership updates until the mismatch is handled elsewhere.\n\nThis is not a float/NaN path; it is a membership publish deadlock that leaves later cycles reading stale `prior` state.\n\n### P3 — Helper quality (**measured**)\n\n- Inner import inside `_compute_membership` on every call.\n- One-line semicolon body and opaque name `r1b_f2_netuids_d` with no docstring, unlike neighboring `get_member_netuids`.\n\nIf the product intent is to omit root from `netuids`, the shrink gate needs an explicit root exception or a migration path; delegating alone is insufficient.\n\n## Skills\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | Traced `validity_map` keys → `r1b_f2_netuids_d` → `build.snapshot.netuids` → `_shrink_allowed` / `_hold_prior` | — |\n| owner-rules | Unsafe-shrink retention must not block all refreshes when only root leaves the list without drop evidence | — |\n| settled-check | `snapshot_coverage` already treats `0 in snap.netuids` as a first-class signal and filters `>0` for scoring separately; omitting 0 from `netuids` without shrink handling re-litigates that boundary | — |\n\n## Verdict\n\n**MODIFY** — align helper semantics with `_shrink_allowed` (or document and implement a root-specific shrink exception) before PASS.",
