      "finalText": "Posted **MODIFY** on PR 9410 at head `bca36052f6be11c67b52c733747a7373cf2ff74a` via `post_verdict`.\n\n**Main issue (inferred):** `r1b_f2_netuids_d` uses `sorted(x for x in keys if x)`, which drops netuid **0** from `netuids` while `\"0\"` can still sit in `validity_map`. The previous line was `sorted(int(k) for k in validity_map.keys())`, which included 0 when present.\n\nThat mismatch hits `_shrink_allowed` in `refresh_once`: removing 0 from `prior.netuids` without a `dropped[0]` entry that passes `_eligible_for_removal` (root never does) blocks the shrink and forces `_hold_prior`. **Inferred** effect for snapshots that already list `0` in `netuids`: refreshes may keep publishing LKG instead of updated membership.\n\nDeclared blocking: `poisons-later-row`.\n\n**Follow-up for the author:** If omitting root from `netuids` is intentional (scoring paths already use `> 0`), add an explicit root exception in `_shrink_allowed` or a migration path—not only this helper.\n\nGate `check_gate_state` still reports `next: review` in the fixture environment; the verdict comment was posted successfully.",
