            "body": "## Summary\n\nOne-line Python change excludes root netuid `0` from `_compute_membership`’s exported `netuids`, matching `load_membership_receipt()` which already builds scoring/export lists with `int(n) > 0` and tracks `root_netuid_in_membership` separately (**measured** in `internal/council/snapshot_coverage.py`). `review-gate-bot/bot/lib/tag.ts` adds only a `pack-b` comment; no tag-epoch or gate logic changes (**measured** in diff).\n\n## Findings\n\n### P2 — `_shrink_allowed` blocks publishing the root-stripped membership (**inferred**)\n\nAfter this diff, a successful build can omit `0` from `build.snapshot.netuids` while netuid `0` remains in `validity_map` (not in `dropped`, because `_eligible_for_removal` is always false for `ROOT_NETUID`). For any prior LKG whose `netuids` still contain `0` (produced by the pre-change line at base), `set(prior.netuids) - set(build.snapshot.netuids)` includes `0`, `build.dropped.get(0)` is `None`, and `_shrink_allowed` returns false → `refresh_once` retains the prior snapshot (**inferred** from `SubnetUniverseProvider.refresh_once` + `_shrink_allowed`). The export fix may never land on disk until manual intervention, despite the membership receipt already treating root as out-of-band.\n\n**Suggested companion:** treat `ROOT_NETUID` like an intentional export shrink in `_shrink_allowed` (skip or always-allow), consistent with the module comment on line 23.\n\n### P3 — PR title vs TS diff (**measured**)\n\nBot “tag metadata sync” is not implemented in TypeScript beyond the comment; behavior change is entirely in Python. Fine if `pack-b` is documentary only; otherwise gate/tag code may still be missing.\n\n## Adversarial extremes\n\nNo new numeric ingress on this diff; `int(k)` on `validity_map` keys is unchanged pre/post. No new overflow/NaN/cycle-abort paths identified.\n\n## Owner alignment (**inferred**)\n\nRoot is explicitly not scored (`membership_scoring_expected` filters `> 0`); exporting `0` in `snap.netuids` was inconsistent with the receipt. Excluding `0` from exported `netuids` matches that standing rule; the shrink gate gap is the main incomplete piece.\n\n## Verdict\n\n**MODIFY** — ship the root exclusion together with a `_shrink_allowed` exception for `ROOT_NETUID`, or an equivalent migration so LKG with `0` can publish the corrected export.",
