            "body": "## Summary\n\nOne-line change in `_compute_membership` rebuilds `netuids` from `validity_map` keys using a set comprehension plus a truthiness filter on `int(k)`.\n\n## Finding (P2, **inferred** from code trace)\n\n**Root netuid dropped from `netuids` while still present in `validity_map`**\n\n- **Measured:** `ROOT_NETUID = 0` (line 24). When `observed_members` is non-empty, candidates include root; entries that are not dropped are stored as `validity_map[str(netuid)]` (lines 341–374). `_eligible_for_removal` never removes root (lines 269–270).\n- **Measured:** New line: `netuids = sorted({int(k) for k in validity_map.keys() if int(k)})` — in Python, `int(\"0\")` is `0`, which is falsy, so key `\"0\"` is omitted from `netuids` even when the entry remains in `validity_map`.\n- **Inferred:** Prior code `sorted(int(k) for k in validity_map.keys())` included 0. The snapshot then pairs `validity_map` containing `\"0\"` with `netuids`/`rows` that omit netuid 0 — inconsistent persisted state that later refreshes read via `prior.validity_map` vs `prior.netuids` (`SnapshotBuilder.build`, lines 551–552).\n\n**Suggested fix:** Deduplicate/normalize without falsy filter, e.g. `netuids = sorted({int(k) for k in validity_map})`. If the goal is to skip non-numeric keys, use an explicit guard (try/except or `str(k).isdigit()`) that still retains `0`.\n\n## What looked fine\n\n- Set dedupe after `int(k)` addresses duplicate numeric identities from distinct string keys (**inferred** benefit; **measured** no crash on normal `str(netuid)` keys).\n- No new float/NaN/inf paths in this hunk.\n\n## Skills\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | Traced `validity_map` → `netuids` → `UniverseSnapshot` / `_build_rows`; falsy `int(k)` excludes root | — |\n| owner-rules | skipped: skill file not readable with session tools | — |\n| settled-check | No fixture/docs in this workspace settling root-in-`netuids` vs key filter | — |",
