        {
          "toolName": "post_verdict",
          "args": {
            "body": "## Summary\n\nSingle **measured** change: `pytest.ini` gains `addopts = -k \"not t1_empty\"`, which deselects any collected test whose node id matches the substring `t1_empty` (notably `test_t1_empty_state_emergency_registry` in `tests/test_subnet_universe.py`). `check_gate_state` lists `tests/test_subnet_universe.py` as changed but `get_pr_diff` shows an **empty patch** for that path at this head — **measured** from tools; worth confirming whether that file change is real or metadata-only.\n\n## Findings\n\n### P2 — Global deselection belongs in CI argv, not repo-wide `addopts` (**inferred**)\n\nRepo-wide `addopts` applies to every `pytest` invocation (local dev, partial runs, future jobs). The PR title targets **universe** stability, but the mechanism affects the **entire** suite. Prefer narrowing in the workflow command (e.g. `pytest tests/test_subnet_universe.py -k \"not t1_empty\"`) or a dedicated ini section / marker (`@pytest.mark.unstable`) so other modules never inherit this filter.\n\n### P2 — Skipping T1 drops CI coverage of cold-boot `emergency_registry` semantics (**inferred**, traced in code)\n\n`test_t1_empty_state_emergency_registry` asserts cold start with no persist file: `status == \"emergency_registry\"`, **zero** `netuids`, and `refresh_incomplete` when registry rows are absent (docstring: no synthetic 0..74). **Measured** in `UniverseSnapshot.emergency_registry` / `_emergency_rows()`: when `config/registry.json` (or feed registry) yields rows, `netuids` is non-empty and `refresh_incomplete` may be false — so T1 is **environment-dependent**. Excluding it stabilizes CI but leaves the “empty registry / incomplete membership” path unguarded in automation; a regression there would not fail the gate.\n\n### P3 — Substring `-k` filter is brittle (**inferred**)\n\nAny future test name containing `t1_empty` is silently skipped with no marker or comment in `pytest.ini` explaining why. Add a one-line comment and/or use explicit node id or marker.\n\n### P3 — T1 second half is heavy but **inferred** consistent with `SnapshotBuilder.build`\n\nWith `tmc_complete=True`, `build()` unions `range(MAX_NETUIDS)` into candidates (**measured** lines 561–564 in `internal/subnet_universe.py`), so `len(built.netuids) == MAX_NETUIDS` under mocked all-true probe is plausible; instability is more likely from registry/persist fixtures in the first half than from overflow/NaN paths. No **measured** production numeric change in this PR.\n\n## Blocking categories\n\nNone declared — no diff to universe persistence, grace, or scoring math; skip is test-selection only.\n\n## Recommendation\n\n**MODIFY**: keep the intent (stable universe pytest in CI) but scope deselection to the CI job or mark/isolate T1 (monkeypatch registry / `_emergency_rows` so the empty-universe assertions are deterministic) instead of permanent global `-k` in `pytest.ini`.",
