      "finalText": "Posted **MODIFY** on [PR 9427](https://github.com/cryptoreporthub/subnet-dashboard/pull/9427) at `c308b207e1d5054a85064ad388414e6ec347e339`.\n\n**What changed (measured):** Only `pytest.ini` adds `addopts = -k \"not t1_empty\"`, which skips `test_t1_empty_state_emergency_registry` (and any other test whose name contains `t1_empty`) on **every** pytest run. `tests/test_subnet_universe.py` is listed as changed but the diff patch at this head is empty.\n\n**Why MODIFY (inferred, no blocking overflow/never-expires items):**\n1. **Scope** — Repo-wide `addopts` is broader than “universe CI”; better to narrow in the workflow or use a marker/isolated fixture.\n2. **Coverage** — T1 guards cold-boot `emergency_registry` with zero netuids when registry is absent; skipping it stabilizes CI but removes automated check of that owner-critical path (`emergency_registry` behavior is environment-sensitive via `_emergency_rows()` / `config/registry.json`).\n3. **Hygiene** — Substring `-k` is brittle; document intent or fix T1 with registry monkeypatch instead of a permanent global skip.\n\nGate `next` remains `review` in the fixture after posting; suite was already **clean**. No production universe code changed in this diff.",
