            ],
            "body": "## Summary\n\nThe PR adds `_token_count_guard` and invokes it at the top of `_eligible_for_removal`, but passes the **literal** `0`, not any per-netuid or audit-trail `token_count`.\n\n## Finding (P1 — blocking)\n\n**Measured:** At head, `_token_count_guard(token_count)` returns `token_count > 0` (`internal/subnet_universe.py`). The new call is `if not _token_count_guard(0): return False`, so the guard always fails and `_eligible_for_removal` **always** returns `False` before root/probe/grace checks.\n\n**Inferred:** Consumers on the real refresh path:\n- `_compute_membership` only records `dropped[netuid]` when `_eligible_for_removal` is true — removals are never recorded.\n- `_shrink_allowed` requires eligibility for every netuid leaving the prior set — shrink is never allowed when membership would shrink.\n- `SubnetUniverseProvider.refresh_once` calls `_shrink_allowed` and `_hold_prior` when shrink is unsafe — the universe **never shrinks**; negative netuids stay in `snap.netuids` past the 48h grace path this function is meant to gate.\n\n**Measured:** `DropEvidence` still has only `tmc`, `probe`, and `negative_since`; there is no `token_count` field and no audit-trail read in this diff despite the PR title.\n\nThis is a **never-expires** class defect: membership rows that should leave after grace cannot become eligible for removal.\n\n## Required fix direction\n\nWire a real non-negative `token_count` from the audit-trail source (and extend `DropEvidence` / drop recording if that is where the count lives), e.g. `_token_count_guard(evidence.token_count)` with defined semantics for `0` (block removal) vs missing data (fail closed per owner rules). Do not pass a constant `0`.\n\n## Extremes (once wired)\n\n**Inferred:** `token_count <= 0` blocks removal via `> 0`; negative counts behave like zero. No float overflow path in the guard itself.",
