      "sessionId": "ses_e684ce6e8068a33947f1ecb7",
      "finalText": "**MODIFY** posted on PR 9440 at `2dbb5f5e435c4aa2b6a6e0497d80367e1beea7bd`.\n\nThe new `_token_count_guard` is only ever called as `_token_count_guard(0)`. Because the guard requires `token_count > 0`, `_eligible_for_removal` always returns `False` immediately. That stops drop evidence from being recorded, makes `_shrink_allowed` reject any shrink, and leaves `refresh_once` holding the prior universe—so netuids never leave membership after the intended 48h grace path. Declared blocking: **never-expires**.\n\nThe diff also does not add `token_count` to `DropEvidence` or connect to any audit-trail source, which does not match the PR title’s intent. Fix by plumbing a real count (and fail-closed semantics for missing/zero) instead of the constant `0`.\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | Constant `0` → eligibility always false on refresh path | — |\n| owner-rules | Shrinks/grace and honest membership require eligible removals | — |\n| settled-check | No settled precedent for this wiring | — |\n\nGate `next` still reads `review` in the fixture environment; the formal MODIFY comment is on the PR.",
