            "body": "## Summary\n\nThe PR title describes capping **RPC batch size** with `max_tokens`, but the only call site applies `_max_tokens_cap` to **`STALE_GRACE_SECONDS`**, not to any batch passed to `ChainReader` / `get_member_netuids`. That miswire changes membership removal timing and persisted universe state.\n\n## Measured\n\n- Diff adds `MAX_TOKENS = 4096`, `_max_tokens_cap(batch, max_tokens=4096) -> min(batch, max_tokens // 2)`, and replaces `>= STALE_GRACE_SECONDS` with `>= _max_tokens_cap(STALE_GRACE_SECONDS)` in `_eligible_for_removal` (`internal/subnet_universe.py`).\n- At head, `STALE_GRACE_SECONDS = 172800` (comment: 48h). `_compute_membership` docstring still says removal happens \"after the 48h grace.\"\n- `_default_probe_fetch` and refresh paths in the same file are unchanged in this diff; no new batch/`max_tokens` use on RPC paths in the patch.\n\n## Inferred\n\n- `_max_tokens_cap(172800)` evaluates to `min(172800, 2048) = 2048`, so a netuid with `probe is False` and a `negative_since` timestamp becomes eligible for drop after ~2048 seconds (~34 minutes), not 172800 seconds (48h).\n- `_eligible_for_removal` feeds `_compute_membership` (`dropped[netuid]`) and `_shrink_allowed` during `refresh_once`; earlier shrink changes what gets published to disk and what `/api/subnets` and pump membership (D5) expose on later cycles — i.e. later rows inherit the wrong grace policy.\n\n## Adversarial trace (real entry: refresh → `_compute_membership` / `_shrink_allowed`)\n\n1. Chain negative sets `negative_since` via `_merge_sources` (unchanged).\n2. Each refresh, `_eligible_for_removal` compares elapsed seconds to `_max_tokens_cap(STALE_GRACE_SECONDS)` → **2048**, not 172800.\n3. Drops accumulate in `dropped`; when `_shrink_allowed` passes, membership shrinks and `_publish` persists the smaller universe.\n\nNo overflow/NaN on this path (integer `min`). Cycle does not abort; the failure mode is **wrong persisted membership timing**, not stuck forever (`never-expires` does not apply).\n\n## Required fix direction\n\n- Restore `_eligible_for_removal` to compare against `STALE_GRACE_SECONDS` unchanged.\n- If RPC batch capping is still desired, wire `_max_tokens_cap` (or equivalent) at the actual batch construction site for chain RPC batches (e.g. where netuid lists are chunked for `ChainReader`), with tests — not on the grace constant.\n\n## Severity\n\nP1 behavioral: contradicts documented 48h grace and PR intent; unsafe shrink timing relative to owner comments in `_merge_sources` (chain negative keeps grace on the row).",
