      "sessionId": "ses_c5d31533c3ff610a3751f06b",
      "finalText": "## Verdict: **MODIFY** (posted)\n\nReviewed head `1016b5cabd566dc8818998e297953f0e935aae8e` on PR [#9441](https://github.com/cryptoreporthub/subnet-dashboard/pull/9441).\n\n**Measured:** The patch adds `_max_tokens_cap(batch) = min(batch, max_tokens // 2)` but the only use is `_max_tokens_cap(STALE_GRACE_SECONDS)` in `_eligible_for_removal`. `STALE_GRACE_SECONDS` is still **172800** (48h). Nothing in the diff touches RPC batching in `_default_probe_fetch` / `ChainReader`.\n\n**Inferred:** The removal threshold becomes **2048 seconds (~34 minutes)** instead of 48 hours. That flows through `_compute_membership` → `_shrink_allowed` → `_publish`, so persisted universe and D5-aligned feeds can shrink on the wrong timeline. Declared blocking: **`poisons-later-row`**.\n\n**Fix direction:** Restore the grace comparison to `STALE_GRACE_SECONDS`. If batch capping is still required, apply it where RPC batches are built, not on the grace constant.\n\nFormal comment is on the PR with the Skills table. Gate fixture still shows `next: review` locally; the channel should pick up the posted MODIFY on the next poll.",
