            "body": "## Summary\n\nSingle-file change in `_compute_membership`: when the registration probe pass is incomplete and a candidate netuid was never placed in `probe_map`, `probe_val` becomes `None` only if `TMC_API_KEY` is present (non-empty after strip); otherwise it becomes `False`.\n\n## Findings\n\n### P1 — Total probe failure + missing `TMC_API_KEY` writes chain-negative validity (**inferred**, **blocking: poisons-later-row**)\n\n**Measured:** `_default_probe_fetch` returns `({}, False)` on head pin failure, RPC failure, or deadline expiry (`internal/subnet_universe.py`).\n\n**Measured:** With `probe_map={}` and `probe_complete=False`, every candidate netuid satisfies `netuid not in probe_map`, so the new branch sets `probe_val=False` whenever `_api_key_present(os.environ.get(\"TMC_API_KEY\"))` is false.\n\n**Inferred:** For prior members with `tmc_positive` true or unknown, `_merge_sources` hits `probe_positive is False and tmc_positive is not False` and returns `validity=\"negative\"` with a fresh `negative_since`. That happens without any successful chain registration observation—only because the probe pass failed empty.\n\n**Inferred:** `refresh_once` → `SnapshotBuilder.build` → `_compute_membership` is the production entry; `_hold_prior` / `_shrink_allowed` do not discard that validity_map on publish when netuids remain listed for grace. Downstream `load_membership_receipt` treats chain-negatives as inactive immediately (`snapshot_coverage.py` comment + logic).\n\n**Ask:** Restrict `False` gap-fill to partial maps (non-empty `probe_map`) or skip gap interpretation when the probe outcome is total failure; add a regression test mirroring `_default_probe_fetch`’s empty incomplete return.\n\n### P2 — PR title vs implementation (**inferred**)\n\nTitle says “read api_key header”; code reads `os.environ.get(\"TMC_API_KEY\")` only. If the product seam is a request header, background refresh will not see it unless env is populated elsewhere—confirm naming/intent.\n\n### P3 — No tests in diff (**measured**)\n\nDiff is logic-only; behavior change for incomplete probe + env key deserves unit coverage via `SnapshotBuilder` injection.\n\n## Positive\n\n**Measured:** `_api_key_present` correctly rejects whitespace-only keys. **Measured:** When `TMC_API_KEY` is set, gap behavior matches base (`None`). **Measured:** `ROOT_NETUID` still forced to `probe_val=None` after the branch.\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | Traced `refresh_once` → `build` → `_compute_membership`; empty failed probe + no env key → mass `probe_val=False` → `_merge_sources` negatives | — |\n| owner-rules | Chain-wins on complete `probe_positive=False` is documented; incomplete empty probe is not a complete chain read | — |\n| settled-check | Fixture repo has no roadmap/locks for this branch; not treated as settled | — |",
