      "finalText": "Posted **MODIFY** on [PR 9442](https://github.com/cryptoreporthub/subnet-dashboard/pull/9442) at `a34965c9e4933b1732040e827aea9a767d98504e`.\n\nThe change gates incomplete-probe gap fill on `TMC_API_KEY`: with a key, missing `probe_map` entries stay `None` (same as base); without a key, they become `False`.\n\n**Blocking concern (`poisons-later-row`):** When `_default_probe_fetch` fails completely it returns an empty map and `probe_complete=False`. With no `TMC_API_KEY`, every candidate hits the new branch and gets `probe_val=False`, so `_merge_sources` can mark widespread chain-negative validity even though no registration read succeeded. That state can persist on publish and feed membership receipts.\n\n**Also noted:** Title mentions an `api_key` header but the code only reads `TMC_API_KEY` from the environment, and the diff has no tests.\n\nGate `next` still reads `review` in this fixture session; the formal MODIFY comment is on the PR for the author to address before PASS.",
