            "body": "## Summary\n\nExtracts membership list building into `r1b_member_netuids_from_map_a` in `internal/run_mode.py` and calls it from `_compute_membership`. The helper is not a pure refactor: it changes semantics from `sorted(int(k) for k in validity_map.keys())` to the same list **with netuid 0 filtered out** (`if int(k)`).\n\n## Findings\n\n### P1 — ROOT (0) dropped from `netuids` while still admitted to `validity_map` (**inferred** from head code + diff)\n\n**Measured:** `ROOT_NETUID = 0` and comment at `internal/subnet_universe.py` L22: membership adds root when there are observed members; `_compute_membership` still does `candidates.add(ROOT_NETUID)` when `observed_members` is non-empty and can write `validity_map[\"0\"]`.\n\n**Measured (diff):** `r1b_member_netuids_from_map_a` returns `sorted(int(k) for k in validity_map.keys() if int(k))`, excluding 0.\n\n**Inferred:** On any refresh where root stays in the map, persisted snapshots can carry `validity_map` containing `\"0\"` while `netuids` and `rows` omit 0 — internal inconsistency later cycles read back.\n\n### P1 — Unsafe shrink when prior LKG listed netuid 0 (**inferred** from real refresh entry `SubnetUniverseProvider.refresh_once` → `_shrink_allowed`)\n\n**Measured:** `_shrink_allowed` requires drop evidence for every `prior.netuids - built.netuids` member; `_eligible_for_removal` returns `False` for `ROOT_NETUID` always (L267–268).\n\n**Inferred:** Deployments whose persisted universe already includes 0 (produced by base behavior) cannot shrink 0 out on refresh; `refresh_once` retains LKG with \"Unsafe shrink blocked\" and never publishes the new membership shape — refresh cycle effectively blocked on upgrade.\n\n### P2 — Helper placement and import (**inferred**)\n\n`internal/run_mode.py` is Fly process-mode configuration; subnet membership policy does not belong there without a documented run-mode seam. Lazy `from internal.run_mode import ...` inside `_compute_membership` adds import work on every membership resolution.\n\n### P2 — No tests in diff (**measured**)\n\nOnly `internal/subnet_universe.py` and `internal/run_mode.py` change; no regression test for root-in-map vs netuids list or shrink transition.\n\n## What would unblock PASS\n\n- Align policy explicitly: if root must not appear in exported `netuids`, also stop persisting `\"0\"` in `validity_map` **or** teach `_shrink_allowed` that ROOT may leave without negative drop evidence; add tests for both fresh build and LKG-with-0 upgrade.\n- If the intent is truly identical behavior to base, remove `if int(k)`.\n\n## Adversarial extremes\n\nNon-numeric `validity_map` keys still raise on `int(k)` (same as base). No new float/`inf` path in this diff; overflow class not implicated.",
