            "body": "## Summary\n\nThe diff centralizes membership netuid extraction in `r1b_member_netuids_from_map_b`, which drops netuid **0** from `validity_map` keys (`if int(k)`), aligning `_compute_membership` with `internal/subnets/tradable.py` and the `ROOT_NETUID` comment (chain `get_member_netuids` never treats root as a member). **Measured:** head replaces `sorted(int(k) for k in validity_map.keys())` with that helper; behavior change is **only** exclusion of **0** when `\"0\"` is present in `validity_map`.\n\n## Findings\n\n### P2 — Root drop can be blocked by `_shrink_allowed` (inferred)\n\n**Measured:** `_compute_membership` still adds `ROOT_NETUID` to `candidates` when `observed_members` is non-empty and can keep a positive `\"0\"` entry in `validity_map`, while the new helper omits **0** from returned `netuids`.\n\n**Measured:** `SnapshotBuilder.build` → `refresh_once` publishes via `_shrink_allowed` / `_hold_prior`. For any `netuid` in `set(prior.netuids) - set(build.snapshot.netuids)`, shrink requires `build.dropped[netuid]` and `_eligible_for_removal` (**measured:** `_eligible_for_removal` returns **False** immediately for `ROOT_NETUID`).\n\n**Inferred:** Deployments whose persisted LKG still has `0` in `prior.netuids` (possible under the **base** one-liner) will produce builds without **0** but fail shrink, retain the prior snapshot, and **keep publishing root in membership** indefinitely. That undercuts the stated generalization without a migration seam (e.g. exempt root from shrink diff, strip root on load, or document a one-time persist bump).\n\n### P3 — Helper polish (inferred)\n\n- No docstring; name `r1b_member_netuids_from_map_b` is opaque next to `is_tradable_subnet` / `membership_scoring_expected`, which use explicit `> 0`.\n- Lazy import inside `_compute_membership` is inconsistent with the rest of `subnet_universe.py` (could be top-level; **measured:** `tradable.py` does not import `subnet_universe`, so no cycle seen in fixture).\n\n## Adversarial extremes\n\n**Measured:** Invalid map keys still raise in `int(k)` — same as base. Empty map → `[]`. No new float/`inf` paths.\n\n**Inferred:** No new abort-only path beyond existing `int(k)` on corrupt keys.\n\n## Owner / settled\n\n**Inferred:** Root must not count as a tradable subnet (`tradable.py` module doc, `snapshot_coverage` `root_netuid_in_membership` telemetry) — direction matches owner intent; shrink interaction needs an explicit decision so the helper actually lands in production.\n\n## Recommendation\n\n**MODIFY:** Keep the helper, but add a shrink/persist seam so root removal from `netuids` is not treated as a grace-gated shrink (or strip `0` when reloading LKG). Add a short docstring and prefer `int(k) > 0` for parity with `is_tradable_subnet`. Consider a focused unit test for `\"0\"` in `validity_map` (not in fixture slice; **guess** full repo may already have universe tests elsewhere).\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | Traced `validity_map` → `_compute_membership` → `SnapshotBuilder` / `_shrink_allowed` / persisted `netuids`; root exclusion vs shrink gate | — |\n| owner-rules | Root exclusion aligns with tradable-universe rules; missing migration conflicts with “root not in membership” | — |\n| settled-check | No roadmap/lock text in fixture; treated as open shrink/LKG interaction | — |",
