      "sessionId": "ses_a5f0ba7a0b26f75f9a2156ea",
      "finalText": "Posted **MODIFY** on head `265a4b46f9dc54e3a7cd7f372235f248139050c3` for [PR 9451](https://github.com/cryptoreporthub/subnet-dashboard/pull/9451).\n\n**Main issue (blocking: `poisons-later-row`):** Base code builds `netuids` from every `validity_map` key, including `\"0\"`. The new helper `r1b_member_netuids_from_map_c` uses `if int(k)`, which drops netuid **0**. `_compute_membership` can still put root in `validity_map` when there are observed members (`ROOT_NETUID = 0`, “membership adds it”), while `load_membership_receipt` treats `0 in snap.netuids` as the signal for root membership. **Inferred:** snapshots can persist `validity_map[\"0\"]` without a matching `netuids`/row entry, and later refreshes can read that split state back.\n\n**Secondary (P3):** Membership logic is pulled into `score_cache` via a function-local import; the new helper has no type hints.\n\nGate `next` still reads `review` in this fixture environment after the post; the formal verdict is on the PR via `post_verdict`.",
