            "body": "## Summary\n\nRefactor extracts membership netuid listing into `r1b_member_netuids_from_map_d` in `internal/chain_price/membership.py` and calls it from `_compute_membership`. That helper is **not** a pure rename: it changes semantics versus base.\n\n## Findings\n\n### P1 — Exported netuids omit netuid 0 (behavior change)\n\n**Measured:** Base `_compute_membership` ended with:\n`netuids = sorted(int(k) for k in validity_map.keys())`.\n\n**Measured:** Head uses:\n`return sorted(int(k) for k in validity_map.keys() if int(k))`, which drops netuid `0` whenever `\"0\"` is present in `validity_map`.\n\n**Measured:** `_compute_membership` still adds `ROOT_NETUID` to `candidates` when `observed_members` is non-empty and can keep root in `validity_map` (root is never eligible for `dropped`). The module comment on `ROOT_NETUID` states chain membership lists drop root while merge logic may still track it.\n\n**Inferred:** Aligning exported `netuids` with `get_member_netuids` (which excludes `netuid != 0`) is plausible for #1395 generalization, but it is a deliberate API/snapshot shape change for `/api/subnets`, pump rows, and `root_netuid_in_membership` telemetry (`0 in snap.netuids` in `snapshot_coverage.py`).\n\n**Ask:** Add a docstring on `r1b_member_netuids_from_map_d` stating that validity-map keys may include root but exported member netuids exclude `0`, matching `get_member_netuids`. Add a focused unit test (map containing `\"0\"` and `\"5\"` → `[5]` only).\n\n### P2 — LKG shrink gate can block forever when prior listed root\n\n**Measured:** `_shrink_allowed` requires `DropEvidence` and `_eligible_for_removal` for every netuid in `prior.netuids - build.snapshot.netuids`. `_eligible_for_removal` returns `False` for `ROOT_NETUID` always.\n\n**Inferred:** After deploy, if persisted LKG `netuids` still contain `0` (produced by base logic) and the new helper omits `0` from `build.snapshot.netuids` without putting `0` in `dropped`, `_shrink_allowed` returns `False` and `refresh_once` retains the prior snapshot (`Unsafe shrink blocked`). The worker may never publish a snapshot consistent with the new helper until the disk file is edited or root disappears from prior for another reason.\n\n**Ask:** Treat omission of root from exported netuids as shrink-safe (e.g. exclude `ROOT_NETUID` from the shrink diff, or document a one-time migration). Without this, generalization can deadlock against existing LKG.\n\n### P3 — Import placement\n\n**Measured:** `from internal.chain_price.membership import r1b_member_netuids_from_map_d` runs inside `_compute_membership` each call.\n\n**Inferred:** Module-level import matches the rest of `subnet_universe.py` and avoids repeated import work on the refresh path.\n\n## Adversarial extremes\n\n**Measured:** Keys in `validity_map` are produced as `str(netuid)` in the membership loop; corrupt non-numeric keys would raise on `int(k)` in both base and head (same abort surface on refresh).\n\n**Measured:** No float/`1e308`/grace multiply paths in this diff.\n\n## Owner rules touched\n\n**Inferred:** Chain/probe merge and 48h grace logic are unchanged; only the netuid list derivation changed. Scoring already ignores root via `membership_scoring_expected(... if int(n) > 0)`.\n\n## Settled check\n\n**Measured:** Fixture slice has no tests or roadmap entry for `r1b_member_netuids_from_map_d`; behavior change is not locked by in-repo tests here.\n\nNot a PASS: semantic change plus shrink/LKG interaction need explicit handling before merge.",
