      "finalText": "Posted **MODIFY** on PR 9452 at head `0b569f846468d4bf9538816cedbc60f8936e75fe`.\n\nThe refactor is not a straight extract: `r1b_member_netuids_from_map_d` uses `if int(k)`, so **netuid 0 is dropped** from exported `netuids` when `\"0\"` is still in `validity_map`. Base used every validity-map key. That matches `get_member_netuids` and the `ROOT_NETUID` comment in spirit, but it changes `/api/subnets`, pump membership rows, and `root_netuid_in_membership` unless you document and test it.\n\n**Shrink / LKG:** If disk LKG still lists `0` (from old logic) and the new helper omits it without a `dropped` entry, `_shrink_allowed` fails because root is never removal-eligible. Refresh can stay on “Unsafe shrink blocked” and never publish a snapshot aligned with the helper.\n\n**Smaller:** Move the import to module scope; add a docstring and a unit test for map `{\"0\": …, \"5\": …} → [5]`.\n\nNo blocking overflow/grace/never-expire issues in this diff; MODIFY is for the semantic and migration gaps above.",
