            "body": "## Summary\n\nSingle-line change in `_compute_membership`: build `netuids` from `validity_map` keys with `if int(k)`, excluding netuid `0` (`ROOT_NETUID`) from the published membership list while the candidate loop still evaluates root for merge/drop logic.\n\n## Trace (adversarial-review)\n\n**Measured:** Diff at head `24f63b5611d21ac6c27ab662c8249a87f83363f6` only touches `internal/subnet_universe.py` line ~378.\n\n**Measured:** Return path is `SnapshotBuilder.build` → `_compute_membership` → `_build_rows(netuids, …)` → `UniverseSnapshot(netuids=…, validity_map=…)` → `get_netuids()` / `get_pump_membership_rows()` / `get_snapshot()`.\n\n**Measured:** `ROOT_NETUID = 0` is still added to `candidates` when `observed_members` is non-empty; probe is forced `None` for root; `_eligible_for_removal` returns `False` for root (unchanged).\n\n**Measured:** `_emergency_rows` already skips `netuid == 0`. `internal/council/snapshot_coverage.py` already filters receipt netuids with `int(n) > 0`, documents that root is never scored, and exposes `root_netuid_in_membership: 0 in snap.netuids` for honesty telemetry.\n\n**Inferred:** After this change, refreshed snapshots should report `root_netuid_in_membership: false` when root would previously have appeared only via membership list inclusion—consistent with scoring and pump/API row lists that never admitted 0.\n\n**Inferred:** `validity_map` may still retain a `\"0\"` entry when the candidate loop keeps root in the map; that pre-dates this one-line filter and does not feed `_build_rows` (rows follow `netuids` only). No production path **measured** here iterates `validity_map` keys as the membership denominator (receipt uses filtered `snap.netuids`).\n\n## Extremes\n\n**Measured:** Keys in `validity_map` originate as `str(netuid)` from sorted integer candidates—non-numeric keys would make `int(k)` raise, same as base.\n\n**Inferred:** `if int(k)` only drops zero; negative netuids remain truthy and are not silent