      "finalText": "Posted **MODIFY** on PR 9454 at `ae2518217bd4ad0d957ff08f88cc0158efd62a6d`.\n\nThe shared helper `r1b_member_netuids_from_map_f` is not equivalent to the line it replaces. Base used `sorted(int(k) for k in validity_map.keys())`, which keeps netuid **0** when `\"0\"` is in the map. The new helper adds `if int(k)`, which drops root while `_compute_membership` can still write `validity_map[\"0\"]`.\n\nThat mismatch matters because `_shrink_allowed` treats any netuid in `prior.netuids` but not in the new build as a shrink and requires grace removal evidence. Root is never eligible for removal, so a prior snapshot that still lists `0` (normal under old behavior) can get stuck on “Unsafe shrink blocked” via `_hold_prior`, and `root_netuid_in_membership` in `load_membership_receipt` no longer matches the old meaning.\n\n**Suggested fix:** make the helper match the old sort exactly, or define root policy end-to-end (including shrink and receipt) and cover it with tests.\n\nBlocking tag: `poisons-later-row`. Gate `next` still reads `review` in the fixture after post; Cursor/Ditto/suite steps follow the usual order once MC is recorded on the PR.",
