          "toolName": "post_verdict",
          "args": {
            "body": "## Summary\n\nSingle-line change in `refresh_once`: when `is_universe_refresh_writer()` is false, the code now calls `reload_from_disk_if_stale()` without returning, so execution falls through to `_refresh_lock` acquisition and the full `_builder.build` / `_publish` path.\n\n## Findings\n\n### 1. Non-writer `refresh_once` can publish (latent until called)\n\n**Measured:** At head, `refresh_once` (non-writer branch) reloads from disk then may acquire `_refresh_lock` and run `_publish` (`internal/subnet_universe.py`). **Measured:** At base, the same branch was `return self.reload_from_disk_if_stale()` and never reached the writer build path.\n\n**Measured:** `is_universe_refresh_writer()` doc: only worker may refresh/publish; web reloads persisted snapshots. **Measured:** `ensure_universe_reader()` doc: \"never refresh/publish.\" **Measured:** Production web entry `ensure_background_refresh()` → `ensure_universe_reader()` → `reload_from_disk_if_stale()` only; it does **not** call `refresh_once`. **Measured:** Worker entry uses `refresh_once` with writer=true, so it skips the changed branch.\n\n**Inferred:** With current traced boot paths, this diff is a no-op in prod split web/worker. **Inferred:** Any future (or test) call to `refresh_once()` on a web process can persist a new `subnet_universe.json`, which worker and scoring read via disk reload — inconsistent with the reader contract and load-separation intent behind the writer gate.\n\n**Guess:** Title \"share refresh work across web and worker\" intends lock-shared refresh, but **measured:** `kick_refresh_async` on non-writer still only reloads and returns; no caller wiring in this PR.\n\n### 2. Owner rules / settled\n\n**Measured:** Owner-aligned comments in `_merge_sources` and `snapshot_coverage` (chain wins, 48h grace) are untouched. **Inferred:** This diff does not directly alter grace or negative-since math. **Guess:** `settled-check` / full `owner-rules` skill files were not readable in this session; no settled doc cited for \"web may co-refresh via lock.\"\n\n### Extremes (adversarial)\n\n**Measured:** No numeric acceptance path changed in this hunk (`1e308`, denormals, etc. N/A). **Inferred:** A web-side `_publish` after a degraded/incomplete build could mark membership `refresh_incomplete` on disk and fail closed admission downstream (`membership_allows_admission`) — poisons later cycles that reload that file.\n\n## Recommendation\n\nClarify intent:\n\n- If web should **not** build: restore early return after reload (or `return self._snapshot` after reload when not participating in lock).\n- If web **should** share refresh: wire non-writer boot/kick paths to `refresh_once`, align docs with `is_universe_refresh_writer` / `ensure_universe_reader`, and add tests for lock sharing.\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | Traced web/worker entry points; non-writer fall-through to `_publish` when `refresh_once` runs | — |\n| owner-rules | Writer-only refresh documented vs new fall-through | — |\n| settled-check | No settled call found in available artifacts for web co-publish | skipped: skill file not loaded in session |",
