      "finalText": "**MODIFY** posted on [PR 9402](https://github.com/cryptoreporthub/subnet-dashboard/pull/9402) at `8595d8fd`.\n\nThe change lets `kick_refresh_async` spawn the kick thread when `UNIVERSE_ASYNC_WEB` is set, even on non-writer (web) processes. **`refresh_once` still treats non-writers as read-only** and only calls `reload_from_disk_if_stale()` — so on typical `RUN_MODE=web` this moves disk reload off the request path but does **not** run TMC/probe refresh or publish. That is the main P2 gap relative to the title unless a paired writer-gate change or `RUN_MODE=worker` on those machines is intended.\n\nSecondary P3: `UNIVERSE_ASYNC_WEB` uses raw env truthiness (`\"0\"` / `\"false\"` would still enable the path), unlike the normalized flags in `run_mode.py`.\n\nNo blocking categories were declared; non-writer publish paths are unchanged, so this hunk alone does not add a new web publish surface.",
