            "body": "## Summary\n\nThe diff correctly relaxes `reload_from_disk_if_stale` so web readers accept worker-persisted snapshots whose `netuids` list is empty when `status` is `ok` or `degraded`. That matches **measured** behavior in `SnapshotBuilder.build`, which can publish a degraded snapshot with `netuids=()` after validation (`internal/subnet_universe.py` ~607–618).\n\n## Findings\n\n### P1 — `_load_initial_snapshot` still rejects the same payloads (**measured**, **poisons-later-row**)\n\nOnly `reload_from_disk_if_stale` was updated. `_load_initial_snapshot` still requires `payload.get(\"netuids\")` to be truthy (~664–667). On a web process cold start with a worker-compacted file on disk (empty `netuids`, `status=\"degraded\"`), the provider bootstraps into `emergency_registry` and sets `_disk_mtime` from that file. Subsequent `reload_from_disk_if_stale` calls return early because `mtime <= self._disk_mtime`, so the new acceptance rule never runs until the worker rewrites the file. The process can keep emergency/stale membership for its whole lifetime despite a valid persisted snapshot — bad state that later API/coverage paths read via `get_snapshot()`.\n\n**Fix:** Apply the same `isinstance` + `(netuids or status in (\"ok\", \"degraded\"))` guard in `_load_initial_snapshot` (and consider a one-line shared helper so the two paths cannot drift again).\n\n### P2 — Empty `netuids` + `status=\"ok\"` on disk is accepted on reload (**inferred**)\n\nThe builder’s empty-membership publish path uses `status=\"degraded\"`, not `ok`. Reload nonetheless accepts any `status in (\"ok\", \"degraded\")` with falsy `netuids`. A malformed or hostile persist file could replace in-memory LKG with an empty `ok` universe. Lower severity than P1; tightening to `degraded` only (if that is the worker contract) or requiring non-empty `validity_map` would reduce surface.\n\n### Adversarial trace (reader entry point)\n\nReal reader path: `ensure_universe_reader()` → `reload_from_disk_if_stale()` (non-writer `refresh_once` also delegates here). **Measured:** after this PR, a mtime-advanced degraded empty-netuids file updates `self._snapshot`. **Measured:** `UniverseSnapshot.from_dict` leaves `netuids` empty even when `validity_map` is populated — downstream `load_membership_receipt` keys off `snap.netuids`, so coverage stays empty until a fuller snapshot arrives (pre-existing schema behavior, not introduced by this hunk).\n\n## Owner / settled\n\n**Inferred:** Aligns with the split where workers publish and web reloads (`is_universe_refresh_writer`). No change to chain-wins / 48h grace logic in this hunk.\n\n## Verdict rationale\n\nDirection is right for hot reload, but the boot path omission leaves a reproducible stale/emergency universe on web restart — MODIFY, not PASS.",
            "headSha": "229a31e307a6d172616e1e63b630bb1ab4a42259",
            "skills": [
