      "sessionId": "ses_1f721da268c193536a51bfc5",
      "finalText": "Posted **MODIFY** on PR [#9403](https://github.com/cryptoreporthub/subnet-dashboard/pull/9403) at head `229a31e`.\n\nThe change to `reload_from_disk_if_stale` is the right idea: the builder can persist a **degraded** snapshot with empty `netuids` after validation, and web readers should pick that up instead of ignoring the file.\n\nThe blocking issue is that **`_load_initial_snapshot` still requires truthy `netuids`**, so on a cold web start the provider can land in `emergency_registry`, pin `_disk_mtime`, and never apply the new reload rule until the worker rewrites the file. That is **poisons-later-row** for the boot path.\n\nRecommended fix: use the same acceptance guard in `_load_initial_snapshot` (ideally one shared helper for both paths). I also noted a lower-severity **inferred** concern: reload accepts empty `netuids` with `status=\"ok\"`, while the builder only publishes empty membership as `degraded`.\n\nGate `next` still reads `review` in this fixture session; MC verdict was posted successfully via `post_verdict`.",
