            "body": "## Summary\n\nSingle-file change in `reload_from_disk_if_stale` (web/read-only path). **Measured:** base required `isinstance(payload, dict) and payload.get(\"netuids\")` before `UniverseSnapshot.from_dict`; head splits the checks and accepts the file when either `netuids` or `rows` is present.\n\n## Entry points traced (**inferred** from `internal/subnet_universe.py` at head)\n\n- `ensure_universe_reader()` → `get_provider().reload_from_disk_if_stale()`\n- Non-writer `refresh_once()` and `kick_refresh_async()` → same reload path\n\nWorker publish still goes through `_publish` / `to_dict()` (both fields). This PR only fixes readers missing a newer on-disk file when `netuids` is temporarily empty during migration but `rows` is already written.\n\n## Adversarial checks\n\n| Input | Outcome |\n| --- | --- |\n| Non-`dict` JSON | Early return; keeps in-memory `_snapshot` (**inferred** safe) |\n| `{}` or dict with neither field | Skips reload (**measured** condition) |\n| `rows` populated, `netuids` missing/`[]` | `from_dict` loads rows; `netuids` tuple empty (**measured** in `from_dict`) |\n| Invalid `netuids` elements | `int(n)` raises; outer `except` logs and retains prior snapshot (**inferred**) |\n\n**Inferred:** A rows-only reload yields empty `get_netuids()` while `get_pump_membership_rows()` can still serve rows—consistent with a mid-migration worker write, not a shrink/eviction path. No change to `_compute_membership`, grace, or chain-wins merge on the writer.\n\n## Non-blocking follow-up (P3)\n\n`_load_initial_snapshot` still requires `payload.get(\"netuids\")` (**measured** at head). Cold-start web could still fall back to `emergency_registry` for the same on-disk shape this reload now accepts. Worth aligning in a follow-up, not a gate blocker.\n\n## Owner / settled\n\n**Inferred:** Matches D5 reader behavior (reload persisted snapshot, never publish) and avoids stale LKG when disk moved ahead during format migration. No re-litigation of ch