      "finalText": "**Verdict: PASS** posted for head `92f5a7759d754a12262f45ac839e0d7167d4a427` on [PR 9404](https://github.com/cryptoreporthub/subnet-dashboard/pull/9404).\n\nThe diff fixes the read-only reload path: `reload_from_disk_if_stale` no longer requires a truthy `netuids` key before calling `UniverseSnapshot.from_dict`. It now accepts on-disk snapshots that only have `rows` during a `netuids` field migration, which matches how `ensure_universe_reader` and non-writer `refresh_once` / `kick_refresh_async` pick up worker-published files.\n\nI traced that path from the public entry points, checked corrupt or partial JSON handling (non-dict, empty payload, bad `netuids` elements), and found no blocking issues under the gate categories. **Inferred** follow-up only: `_load_initial_snapshot` still insists on `netuids` on cold start, so the same mid-migration file shape might still fall back to `emergency_registry` until a stale reload runs—worth aligning later, not a blocker for this narrow fix.\n\nGate fixture still shows `next: review` and MC as missing; the verdict was accepted by `post_verdict`. The channel should advance Cursor/Ditto and suite per `lib/gate.ts` once the posted comment is visible on the PR.",
