            "body": "## Summary\n\nOne-line gate change in `_load_initial_snapshot` so persisted LKG is accepted when `rows` is present even if `netuids` is empty/cleared. **Measured:** diff only touches the load predicate at `internal/subnet_universe.py` (~658). **Inferred:** the stated scenario still produces an internally inconsistent `UniverseSnapshot` and leaves the reader reload path unchanged.\n\n## Findings\n\n### P2 — Load predicate fixed; snapshot shape still wrong for cleared `netuids` (blocking: poisons-later-row)\n\n**Measured:** `_load_initial_snapshot` now accepts `(payload.get(\"netuids\") or payload.get(\"rows\"))` and calls `UniverseSnapshot.from_dict(payload)`.\n\n**Measured:** `UniverseSnapshot.from_dict` sets `netuids` only from `payload.get(\"netuids\") or []` — it does **not** derive membership IDs from `rows` or `validity_map` keys.\n\n**Inferred:** For the PR title scenario (`netuids: []`, non-empty `rows`, often intact `validity_map`), startup returns a snapshot with **empty `netuids`** but **non-empty `rows`/map**. Downstream:\n- `get_netuids()` / `load_membership_receipt()` (via `snap.netuids`) see **empty membership**.\n- `get_pump_membership_rows()` still serves **row data** from `snap.rows`.\n- `SnapshotBuilder.build` seeds `prior_members` from `prior.netuids` only (`prior_members = set(prior.netuids)`), so the **first refresh** after boot treats prior membership as empty even when `validity_map` still describes removed/challenged netuids — grace and hold-prior logic tied to prior IDs can be skipped or rebuilt from scratch.\n\nThat is inconsistent shared state that later refresh/scoring cycles read back; it matches the gate’s **poisons-later-row** bar for this path enabled by the new accept condition.\n\n**Suggested fix:** When `netuids` is missing/empty but `rows` (and/or `validity_map`) remain, reconcile `netuids` inside `from_dict` (e.g. union of row netuids and map keys) before returning; or apply the same `(netuids or rows)` acceptance and reconciliation in one helper used by both load paths.\n\n### P2 — Reader reload path still rejects the same files\n\n**Measured:** `reload_from_disk_if_stale` still requires `payload.get(\"netuids\")` truthy before `from_dict` (~681–684 at head). Web/read-only processes that only reload disk will **not** pick up the cleared-`netuids`/intact-`rows` files this PR is meant to accept on worker boot.\n\n**Suggested fix:** Share the same usability predicate (and reconciliation) between `_load_initial_snapshot` and `reload_from_disk_if_stale`.\n\n### P3 — Truthy non-list `rows` passes the gate\n\n**Inferred:** Any truthy `rows` value (e.g. a string) satisfies the new OR condition; `from_dict` then yields empty parsed rows. Prefer `isinstance(payload.get(\"rows\"), list) and payload[\"rows\"]` (and/or non-empty reconciled netuids) before treating persistence as usable.\n\n## What looks fine\n\n**Measured:** No float/overflow/expiry paths touched; change is JSON load gating only. **Inferred:** No new cycle-abort or never-expire behavior in this diff.\n\n## Test plan (author)\n\n- Persist fixture: `netuids: []`, populated `rows`, non-trivial `validity_map`; assert `_load_initial_snapshot` and `reload_from_disk_if_stale` both yield reconciled `netuids` aligned with rows/map.\n- Assert first `SnapshotBuilder.build` after load retains prior grace for netuids present only in map/rows.\n- Regression: normal files with non-empty `netuids` unchanged.",
