      "finalText": "Review for [PR 9406](https://github.com/cryptoreporthub/subnet-dashboard/pull/9406) at `c3547ea757c657fc0d34145feb1745b9a51a0773` is posted: **MODIFY**.\n\nThe one-line change correctly stops rejecting LKG files when `netuids` is empty but `rows` is present. **Inferred:** that is not enough for the title scenario, because `UniverseSnapshot.from_dict` still builds an empty `netuids` tuple from the payload while `rows` (and often `validity_map`) stay populated. That splits consumers (`get_netuids` / membership receipts vs pump rows) and makes `SnapshotBuilder.build` treat `prior_members` as empty on the first refresh, which can drop grace tied to prior IDs (**poisons-later-row**).\n\nAlso **measured:** `reload_from_disk_if_stale` still requires truthy `netuids`, so web reload paths will not accept the same files worker boot now loads.\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | Load → `from_dict` → refresh/scoring paths; cleared `netuids` + intact rows | — |\n| owner-rules | Shared universe must stay consistent across API, pump, scoring | — |\n| settled-check | Change targets prior “no netuids → emergency” behavior; reconciliation not settled elsewhere | — |\n\nSuggested follow-up: reconcile `netuids` from `rows`/`validity_map` in one shared helper used by both load and reload, plus a persistence fixture test.",
