            "body": "## Summary\n\nPR wires `_compute_membership` to `r1b_f2_netuids_c(validity_map)` instead of `sorted(int(k) for k in validity_map.keys())`, centralizing the positive-netuid key shape already used in `membership_scoring_expected` / `load_membership_receipt` (`int(n) > 0`).\n\n## Findings\n\n### P2 — `validity_map` vs `netuids` divergence (blocking)\n\n**Measured:** `r1b_f2_netuids_c` (from diff) is:\n```python\nreturn sorted(k for k in (int(x) for x in validity_map) if max(k, 0))\n```\nFor integer keys this is equivalent to `k > 0`, so netuid `0` is never included even when `_compute_membership` still writes `validity_map[\"0\"]` (ROOT is explicitly added to candidates when `observed_members` is non-empty; see `ROOT_NETUID` comment at line 23).\n\n**Inferred:** When the only remaining validity entry is root (`validity_map == {\"0\": ...}`), the old path returned `netuids=[0]` and `_build_rows` produced a snapshot; the new path returns `netuids=[]`, which drives `SnapshotBuilder.build` through the empty-membership branch and can persist `netuids=()` while `validity_map` still contains `\"0\"` (see empty snapshot return around the degraded \"Membership resolved empty\" path). A later refresh reads that inconsistent pair from disk — bad state carried forward.\n\n**Inferred:** For normal multi-subnet universes, behavior matches the coverage export shape (positive IDs only). Side effects: `0 in snap.netuids` / `root_netuid_in_membership` will no longer be true on freshly built snapshots even when root remains in `validity_map`; API rows no longer include a root row when root was only carried via membership logic.\n\n### P3 — Helper clarity / DRY\n\n**Inferred:** `max(k, 0)` as a truthiness filter is easy to misread versus `k > 0` used elsewhere in `snapshot_coverage.py`. The helper could delegate to `membership_scoring_expected([int(x) for x in validity_map])` to lock one implementation (no test files in this diff slice).\n\n### P3 — Import placement\n\n**Measured:** Function-local import of `r1b_f2_netuids_c` inside `_compute_membership` avoids eager `subnet_universe` ↔ `snapshot_coverage` import cycles (`load_membership_receipt` already imports `subnet_universe` lazily). Acceptable pattern.\n\n## Extremes (adversarial)\n\n**Measured:** Invalid map keys still raise on `int(x)` — same as before. **Inferred:** No float overflow path here (integer netuids only). **Inferred:** No row-expiry / scoring-cycle abort from this change on typical positive membership sets.\n\n## Verdict\n\nAligning export shape with coverage is the right direction, but the positive-only filter must not leave a non-empty `validity_map` paired with an empty `netuids` list (or drop/update the root validity entry in the same breath). Resync root handling (`root_netuid_in_membership`, rows) or add a regression test for root-only / root-in-map cases.\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | Traced `_compute_membership` → `SnapshotBuilder.build` → persisted snapshot; compared to `membership_scoring_expected` / receipt filtering | — |\n| owner-rules | Applied inline owner semantics: root added to membership, scoring/coverage positive-only, fail-closed admission | — |\n| settled-check | skipped: fixture slice has no locks/roadmap docs to search | — |",
