      "finalText": "Posted **MODIFY** on [PR 9409](https://github.com/cryptoreporthub/subnet-dashboard/pull/9409) at head `3a543a09ff0a1d85e96578ad956e77cfd2a83319`.\n\n**Why not PASS:** `r1b_f2_netuids_c` filters with `max(k, 0)`, which for ints means **netuid 0 is dropped** even when `_compute_membership` still keeps `\"0\"` in `validity_map` (root is still added to candidates when there are observed members). **Measured:** that differs from the old `sorted(int(k) for k in validity_map.keys())`. **Inferred:** if `\"0\"` is the only validity entry, `netuids` becomes `[]` while `validity_map` can still hold `\"0\"`, and `SnapshotBuilder.build` can persist that mismatch for the next cycle — declared as blocking **`poisons-later-row`**.\n\n**What works:** For normal positive membership, this matches the coverage export shape (`membership_scoring_expected` / receipt `int(n) > 0`). The local import avoids an import cycle with `load_membership_receipt`.\n\n**Ask for the author:** Keep `validity_map` and exported `netuids` in sync when root is handled (or adjust root telemetry / rows), prefer `k > 0` or reuse `membership_scoring_expected`, and add a test for root-in-map / root-only edge cases.\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | Traced `_compute_membership` → build → persist | — |\n| owner-rules | Root + positive-only scoring semantics | — |\n| settled-check | skipped: no lock docs in fixture | — |",
