          "args": {
            "body": "## Summary\n\nPR delegates `_compute_membership` netuid ordering to `internal.chain_price.membership.r1b_f2_netuids_d`. The helper changes membership output in a way that conflicts with existing universe semantics and downstream telemetry.\n\n## Findings\n\n### P1 — `r1b_f2_netuids_d` silently drops root netuid 0 (**inferred** from code; behavior vs base **measured** via `read_repo_file` at head/base)\n\n**Base** (`internal/subnet_universe.py` at base): `netuids = sorted(int(k) for k in validity_map.keys())` — every validity_map key, including `\"0\"`, becomes a member ID.\n\n**Head** helper:\n```python\ndef r1b_f2_netuids_d(validity_map):\n    keys = [int(k) for k in validity_map.keys()]; return sorted(x for x in keys if x)\n```\nThe `if x` filter removes falsy integers, so **netuid 0 is never returned** even when `validity_map[\"0\"]` exists.\n\n**Entry path (inferred):** `_compute_membership` adds `ROOT_NETUID` (0) to `candidates` when `observed_members` is non-empty (measured at head lines 336–338, 23). Positive root entries remain in `validity_map` unless dropped; only the netuid list is filtered.\n\n**Consumers (measured):**\n- `SnapshotBuilder.build` → `_build_rows(netuids, …)` builds `/api/subnets` and pump rows only for IDs in `netuids` — root row disappears while `validity_map` may still describe root.\n- `load_membership_receipt` in `internal/council/snapshot_coverage.py` exposes `\"root_netuid_in_membership\": 0 in snap.netuids` — this flips to false whenever root is only carried via validity_map logic, misreporting membership honesty.\n- Persisted snapshots (`to_dict` / disk) can store `validity_map` with `\"0\"` but `netuids` without `0`; later refreshes read `prior.netuids` and `prior.validity_map` separately (**poisons-later-row**).\n\n**Fix direction:** If the intent is “sort validity_map keys”, use the same set as base: `sorted(int(k) for k in validity_map.keys())` (or `sorted(keys)` without truthiness filtering). If the intent is to mirror `get_member_netuids` (exclude 0 from the list), that must be an explicit product decision: update validity_map handling, rows, shrink rules, and `root_netuid_in_membership` together, with tests.\n\n### P3 — Style/maintainability\n\n- One-line helper with semicolon; function-local import in `_compute_membership` hot path (minor).\n\n## Skills\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | Traced validity_map → netuids → rows, persist, coverage receipt | — |\n| owner-rules | Chain-wins merge rule unchanged; no new float paths | — |\n| settled-check | Scoring already excludes 0 via `membership_scoring_expected(>0)`; does **not** settle dropping 0 from `snap.netuids` | — |\n\nNo suite run (read-only review).",
