      "finalText": "**MODIFY** posted for head `bca36052f6be11c67b52c733747a7373cf2ff74a`.\n\nThe new helper `r1b_f2_netuids_d` uses `sorted(x for x in keys if x)`, which **drops netuid 0** because `if 0` is false in Python. Base code used `sorted(int(k) for k in validity_map.keys())`, so root could appear in `netuids` whenever `validity_map[\"0\"]` existed.\n\nThat mismatch matters on the real path: `_compute_membership` can still put root in `validity_map`, but `SnapshotBuilder` builds rows only from `netuids`, and `load_membership_receipt` reports `root_netuid_in_membership` as `0 in snap.netuids`. Persisted snapshots can therefore carry `\"0\"` in `validity_map` while omitting 0 from `netuids` — declared as **poisons-later-row**.\n\nRecommended fix: sort all validity_map keys (no truthiness filter), or, if root should be excluded like `get_member_netuids`, change validity_map, rows, shrink logic, telemetry, and tests together.\n\nGate `next` still reads `review` in the fixture after posting; Cursor/Ditto have not run yet on this head.",
