            "body": "## Summary\n\nTwo-file PR: (1) exclude root netuid from `_compute_membership`’s exported `netuids` list while keeping root in `validity_map`; (2) a comment in `tag.ts` referencing pack-b / tag epoch.\n\n## Findings\n\n### P2 — Root drop blocked by `_shrink_allowed` (**inferred**, blocking)\n\n**Measured:** `ROOT_NETUID = 0` stays in `validity_map` (root cannot be `_eligible_for_removal`). Head change builds `netuids` without `\"0\"`:\n\n```python\nnetuids = sorted(int(k) for k in validity_map.keys() if k != str(0))\n```\n\n**Measured:** `refresh_once` rejects any build whose `netuids` shrinks without per-netuid drop evidence:\n\n```python\nfor netuid in set(prior.netuids) - set(build.snapshot.netuids):\n    evidence = build.dropped.get(netuid)\n    if evidence is None or not _eligible_for_removal(netuid, evidence, now):\n        return False\n```\n\n**Inferred:** Typical LKG snapshots already include `0` in `prior.netuids` (old line included every `validity_map` key). After this change, `built.netuids` omits `0` but `build.dropped` will not carry eligible evidence for netuid `0` (`_eligible_for_removal` returns false for root). `_shrink_allowed` fails → `_hold_prior` → persisted/API `snap.netuids` keeps root indefinitely, so the membership export alignment this PR targets (`load_membership_receipt` already scores `int(n) > 0` only) may not land on worker refresh for existing deployments.\n\n**Suggested fix:** Treat `ROOT_NETUID` as exempt in `_shrink_allowed` (or otherwise allow omitting root from `netuids` without grace evidence), and add/adjust a regression test around refresh from an LKG that still lists `0`.\n\n### P3 — `tag.ts` change is comment-only (**measured**)\n\nThe only diff in `review-gate-bot/bot/lib/tag.ts` is `// pack-b: membership export shares tag epoch with universe refresh`. No gate logic, marker, or epoch field changes. Title/comment imply runtime sync that is not implemented in this diff (**inferred** doc drift only).\n\n### P3 — Prefer `ROOT_NETUID` over `str(0)` (**guess**)\n\nFilter could use `int(k) != ROOT_NETUID` for consistency with the rest of `subnet_universe.py`.\n\n## Positive alignment (**measured**)\n\n`load_membership_receipt()` already derives scoring netuids with `int(n) > 0` and exposes `root_netuid_in_membership: 0 in snap.netuids`. Excluding root from `snap.netuids` matches `membership_scoring_expected` and the file header comment that root is membership metadata, not a probed subnet row.\n\n## Extremes / numeric paths\n\nNo new float/time multiply paths in this diff. Refresh failure mode here is logical (shrink guard), not `1e308`/overflow.\n\n## Settled-check\n\nExcluding root from scoring denominator is already settled in `snapshot_coverage.membership_scoring_expected`. The interaction with `_shrink_allowed` on rollout is not settled in this diff.\n\n## Verdict rationale\n\nCore idea is correct, but without a shrink-guard exception the head change may never publish over real LKG — **MODIFY**, not PASS.",
