      "finalText": "**Verdict posted: PASS** on head `af9a6e08d6e0d56608d0b93aa35e479daa825d20` for [PR 9412](https://github.com/cryptoreporthub/subnet-dashboard/pull/9412).\n\n### Change\nAt the end of `_compute_membership`, membership IDs are built from `validity_map` keys:\n\n```python\nnetuids = sorted({int(k) for k in validity_map.keys() if int(k)})\n```\n\n(replaces a plain sorted list comprehension over `int(k)`.)\n\n### Review conclusion\n- **Deduping via `{int(k) ...}`** (**inferred**): avoids duplicate netuids when two string keys map to the same integer, which could duplicate rows in `_build_rows` and affect pump/API membership.\n- **`if int(k)`** (**inferred**): drops netuid `0` (`ROOT_NETUID`) from the published list while root can still appear in `validity_map`; this matches patterns elsewhere (e.g. emergency rows skip `0`, `snapshot_coverage` uses `int(n) > 0` on `snap.netuids`).\n- **Shrink / LKG** (**inferred**): omitting `0` without drop evidence still goes through `_shrink_allowed`; unsafe shrink is blocked rather than aborting refresh.\n- No blocking issues under the gate categories (overflow, abort cycle, never-expire, poison later row).\n\nNon-blocking nits in the verdict comment: prefer explicit `int(k) > 0` / `!= ROOT_NETUID` over truthiness, and a small test for normalize/dedupe would help.\n\nGate fixture still shows `next: review` and `mc: missing` after post; in production the posted PASS should advance the gate to await Cursor/Ditto. I did not tag reviewers or merge.",
