            "body": "## Summary\n\nTwo-file CI/test-only PR at `e4e74d5`: global `pytest.ini` deselect for `test_t1_empty_state_emergency_registry`, and `@pytest.mark.skip(reason=\"shard timing\")` on `test_t9_chain_unregistered_beats_tmc_listing`. No production code changes (**measured** from diff). Gate suite for this head is **clean** (**measured** via `check_gate_state`).\n\n## Findings\n\n### P2 — Global `addopts` deselect is broader than “every shard”\n\n**measured:** Head `pytest.ini` adds:\n`addopts = --deselect tests/test_subnet_universe.py::test_t1_empty_state_emergency_registry`\n\n**inferred:** That applies to every pytest invocation that reads repo `pytest.ini`, not only sharded CI jobs. The PR title targets shard coverage, but this permanently drops T1 everywhere unless a job overrides `addopts`.\n\n**measured:** T1 combines (a) fast cold-boot `emergency_registry` assertions and (b) a `SnapshotBuilder(...).build(None)` leg asserting `len(built.netuids) == MAX_NETUIDS` with `MAX_NETUIDS = 200` (**measured** in `internal/subnet_universe.py`).\n\n**inferred:** If the goal is shard wall-clock, deselect or skip only the slow builder leg (or gate deselect on a shard env var in CI), not the whole test via global ini.\n\n**measured:** Partial overlap exists (`test_cold_start_empty_tmc_emergency_registry`, `test_cold_start_empty_tmc_emergency_registry_via_provider`, `test_build_probes_full_range_when_tmc_complete`) but none is a single test that ties cold emergency_registry to a full-width cold build like T1’s second half.\n\n### P2 — `test_t9` permanently skipped while expanding universe execution on shards\n\n**measured:** `test_t9_chain_unregistered_beats_tmc_listing` is skipped on all runs; docstring cites owner rule (2026-10-25) chain-over-TMC with 48h grace.\n\n**measured:** T9 body uses mocked `SnapshotBuilder` only—no `time.sleep`, deadlines, or threading (**inferred** from file read at head).\n\n**inferred:** Skip reason `\"shard timing\"` does not match the visible test structure; likely mis-targeted or copy-pasted. Other tests exercise chain-negative paths (`test_complete_chain_read_beats_a_failed_tmc_read`, `test_chain_unregistered_tmc_listed_row_leaves_after_grace_and_stays_gong`, etc.) but T9 is the explicitly labeled owner-rule T9 slot.\n\n**inferred:** Prefer run T9 on one shard (or unskip and fix the real flake) instead of a global skip while rolling universe tests out to every shard.\n\n## Adversarial / production safety\n\n**measured:** Diff touches only `pytest.ini` and `tests/test_subnet_universe.py`. No changes to `_merge_sources`, `_compute_membership`, grace expiry, or provider publish paths.\n\n**inferred:** No new path for never-expiring rows, float overflow, cycle abort, or cross-row poison from this diff.\n\n## Requested follow-up\n\n1. Scope T1 deselect to sharded CI (env-gated) or split T1 and skip/deselect only the `MAX_NETUIDS` cold-build assertions on shards.\n2. Remove global skip on T9 or restrict to redundant shard indices; align skip reason with actual failure mode.\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | Traced changed values (deselect/skip) through pytest entry only; no production consumers | — |\n| owner-rules | T9 documents chain-wins grace; global skip weakens explicit owner-rule CI slot | — |\n| settled-check | No roadmap/docs in fixture slice for shard deselect policy | — |",
