      "finalText": "Posted **MODIFY** on [PR 9422](https://github.com/cryptoreporthub/subnet-dashboard/pull/9422) at `e4e74d5`.\n\nThis is a test-only change: no edits to universe membership or grace logic. The gate still reports a clean suite for this head.\n\n**Why MODIFY (not FAIL)**\n\n1. **Global `pytest.ini` deselect for T1** — The PR title is about running universe tests on every shard, but `addopts = --deselect …test_t1_empty_state_emergency_registry` applies to all pytest runs that use this config, not just sharded CI. T1 mixes fast cold-boot `emergency_registry` checks with a slower cold `SnapshotBuilder` leg that asserts full `MAX_NETUIDS` (200) membership. Better options: split the test and only skip/deselect the slow half on shards, or gate the deselect on a CI shard env var.\n\n2. **`test_t9` skipped everywhere** — T9 is the labeled owner-rule test (chain beats TMC listing, 48h grace). It is mocked and has no obvious timing in the body, so `\"shard timing\"` looks misaligned. Other tests cover similar chain-negative behavior, but skipping T9 globally while expanding universe tests to every shard drops the explicit T9 slot from CI.\n\nNo blocking production findings (`never-expires`, `overflow`, `aborts-cycle`, `poisons-later-row`); the concern is CI scope and coverage hygiene.\n\n**Next gate step:** `review` (fixture still shows MC as missing until the posted comment is picked up; Cursor/Ditto still pending on this head).",
