            "body": "## Summary\n\n**Measured:** `check_gate_state` at `41e0389…` shows two changed paths (`pytest.ini`, `tests/test_subnet_universe.py`), `suite: clean`, `next: review`, no prior MC verdict at this SHA.\n\n**Measured:** The only functional diff is `pytest.ini` adding `addopts = -k \"not sn7_off_chain\"`. Base `pytest.ini` had only `[pytest]` and `pythonpath = .`.\n\n**Measured:** `get_pr_diff` reports `tests/test_subnet_universe.py` as modified with zero additions/deletions and an empty patch; head and base text around `test_sn7_off_chain_but_tmc_listed_leaves_expected_at_127_and_keeps_its_row` match (same owner-rule docstring and assertions).\n\n## Adversarial trace\n\nNo production modules change on this head. The new `addopts` affects pytest collection only; it does not feed runtime config, membership refresh, or API handlers (**inferred** from reading `internal/subnet_universe.py` header and unchanged test/production paths in the fixture).\n\n**Measured:** The deselected test name contains the substring `sn7_off_chain` (`test_sn7_off_chain_but_tmc_listed_…`). Chain-merge / owner-rule coverage remains in the default suite via tests such as `test_t9_chain_unregistered_beats_tmc_listing`, `test_chain_unregistered_tmc_listed_row_leaves_after_grace_and_stays_gone`, `test_complete_chain_read_beats_a_failed_tmc_read`, and related registration/grace tests (**measured** from `read_repo_file` at head).\n\n**Inferred:** Default CI and local `pytest` runs will no longer execute the SN7 + `snapshot_coverage.load_membership_receipt()` integration test unless collection is overridden (e.g. explicit `-k sn7_off_chain`). That matches the PR title intent (focus default universe runs on chain-merge cases) but is worth knowing for anyone relying on that receipt assertion in every run.\n\n## Findings (non-blocking)\n\n| Sev | Finding | Label |\n|-----|---------|-------|\n| P3 | Global `addopts` deselects by name substring rather than a `@pytest.mark`; only one test 