            "body": "MODIFY\n\nReviewed head `c4ed1e8c6a3dd3c00c706bf68e2af4be9c6a751b` (2 files: `pytest.ini`, `tests/test_subnet_universe.py`). **Measured:** gate reports suite `clean` at this head; diff adds a repo-wide pytest `addopts --deselect` for `test_sn7_off_chain_but_tmc_listed_leaves_expected_at_127_and_keeps_its_row` and marks `test_t1_empty_state_emergency_registry` with `@pytest.mark.skip(reason=\"bootstrap ordering\")`. **Measured:** no changes under `internal/subnet_universe.py` or council production code in this PR.\n\n### P2 — Global deselect removes standing owner-rule coverage\n\n**Measured:** `test_sn7_off_chain_but_tmc_listed_leaves_expected_at_127_and_keeps_its_row` builds a disputed chain-negative SN7, keeps the row in membership, then calls `internal.council.snapshot_coverage.load_membership_receipt()` after patching `get_snapshot` and asserts `len(expected_netuids)==127`, `7 not in expected`, `inactive_netuids==[7]` — the same “chain wins / expected drops while row keeps grace” rule documented in `load_membership_receipt`.\n\n**Inferred:** Putting that test in `pytest.ini` `addopts --deselect` disables it for every default pytest invocation (local and CI), not only under xdist workers. Parallel CI hygiene should not permanently drop the only test that ties universe validity to council `expected_netuids`.\n\n**Guess:** The flake is cross-worker pollution on the process-global `get_provider()` singleton despite autouse `_reset_provider_for_tests`; if so, scope isolation with an xdist group / serial job / targeted marker beats a global deselect.\n\n### P3 — Skipped T1 with overlapping coverage\n\n**Measured:** `test_t1_empty_state_emergency_registry` is skipped; cold-start emergency behavior is still exercised by `test_cold_start_empty_tmc_emergency_registry`, `test_cold_start_empty_tmc_emergency_registry_via_provider`, and `test_emergency_rows_empty_without_registry`.\n\n**Inferred:** Skip is tolerable for gate green under parallel bootstrap ordering, but the reason is vague and T1’s explicit `SnapshotBuilder(...).build(None)` → `MAX_NETUIDS` membership path is slightly less duplicated elsewhere.\n\n### Adversarial trace (production entry points)\n\n**Measured:** Changed values are pytest config and skip metadata only; they do not alter `SubnetUniverseProvider.refresh_once`, `_compute_membership`, or `_merge_sources`. **Inferred:** No new path for `1e308`, `inf`, `NaN`, or grace never-expiring from this diff.\n\n### Title vs diff\n\n**Measured:** PR title references parallelizing the universe suite; this head’s file list contains no workflow or xdist wiring—only deselect/skip. **Inferred:** Either parallelization lives outside this diff or the title oversells a harness-only change; worth aligning docs/CI comments with what actually ships.\n\nNo blocking production defects (`never-expires`, `overflow`, `aborts-cycle`, `poisons-later-row`) identified in changed code.",
