            "body": "## Summary\n\nSingle functional change: repo-wide `pytest.ini` adds `addopts = -k \"not t1_empty\"`, which deselects `test_t1_empty_state_emergency_registry` (and any future test whose node id contains `t1_empty`) on **every** default pytest invocation. `tests/test_subnet_universe.py` is listed as modified but the PR patch is empty (**measured** via `get_pr_diff`); head/base reads of T1 match (**measured**).\n\n## Findings\n\n### P2 — Global deselection vs “universe collect” scope (**inferred**)\n\nThe PR title targets universe pytest collect, but `addopts` in root `pytest.ini` applies to the full suite, not a universe-only job or `tests/test_subnet_universe.py` path. Today only T1 matches the substring filter; the mechanism still hides T1 from local `pytest`, gate suite runs, and CI unless callers override `-o addopts=` or pass an explicit `-k`.\n\n### P2 — T1 covers fail-closed cold boot; skipping it removes explicit coverage (**inferred**)\n\nTraced T1 through the real provider entry: `SubnetUniverseProvider._load_initial_snapshot()` → `UniverseSnapshot.emergency_registry(reason=…)` when persistence is missing (**measured** in `internal/subnet_universe.py`). T1 asserts empty `netuids`, `refresh_incomplete`, and `emergency_registry` on cold boot (docstring: missing gitignored registry, no synthetic 0..74). That aligns with `membership_allows_admission()` rejecting `universe_status == \"emergency_registry\"` in `internal/council/snapshot_coverage.py` (**measured**). Excluding T1 by default means the suite no longer exercises that documented owner behavior unless someone opts in.\n\n**inferred:** T1’s first half is environment-sensitive (registry rows via `_emergency_rows()` / `registry_subnet_rows()`), which plausibly motivates CI instability; the fix should stabilize the test (e.g. monkeypatch registry rows empty for that case) or narrow deselection to the CI job that collects universe tests—not a permanent global `-k`.\n\n### P3 — Opaque one-line ini change (**measured**)\n\nNo comment in `pytest.ini` tying the filter to flake/collect rationale or to an explicit manual run (`pytest -k t1_empty`). Future readers will not know T1 is intentionally out of default runs.\n\n## Adversarial trace (production paths)\n\nNo production code changed. `addopts` affects test collection only; no float/`MAX_NETUIDS` overflow, row expiry, or cross-cycle poison paths are introduced by this diff.\n\n## Suite\n\nGate reports suite **clean** at this head (**measured**); carry-over not required for this review.\n\n## Recommendation\n\nPrefer stabilizing T1 under CI (isolate registry/emergency fixtures) or scoping `-k \"not t1_empty\"` to the universe CI step. If global skip remains, document it in `pytest.ini` and add a targeted marker plus a scheduled/manual job that still runs T1.",
