      "finalText": "Posted **MODIFY** on [PR 9427](https://github.com/cryptoreporthub/subnet-dashboard/pull/9427) at head `c308b207e1d5054a85064ad388414e6ec347e339`.\n\n**What changed (measured):** Only `pytest.ini` gains `addopts = -k \"not t1_empty\"`, which drops `test_t1_empty_state_emergency_registry` from default pytest runs repo-wide. The universe test file is listed in the PR but has no patch; T1 at head matches base.\n\n**Why MODIFY (inferred, not blocking runtime):**\n- Repo-wide `addopts` is broader than “universe collect” and hides T1 locally and in CI unless overridden.\n- T1 is the explicit cold-boot `emergency_registry` / empty-membership case that lines up with fail-closed scoring admission; skipping it by default removes that coverage without stabilizing the test (e.g. empty registry fixture) or scoping the filter to the CI job.\n- The ini line has no comment explaining intent or how to run T1 on purpose.\n\nNo blocking items (`never-expires`, `overflow`, `aborts-cycle`, `poisons-later-row`) — production paths are untouched.\n\nGate `next` still reads `review` in the session fixture; formal MC comment is on the PR. Next step in order is **Cursor** review at this SHA, then Ditto, then suite (already clean), Replit tag, etc.",
