            "body": "## Summary\n\nThe diff adds `_token_count_guard` and an early check in `_eligible_for_removal`, but the call site passes the **literal** `0`, not any audit-trail or per-netuid `token_count`. **Measured:** `_token_count_guard` returns `token_count > 0` (`internal/subnet_universe.py` at head). **Measured:** the new branch is `if not _token_count_guard(0): return False`. **Inferred:** for every call, `0 > 0` is false, so `_eligible_for_removal` always returns false before probe/grace checks run.\n\n## Entry-point trace\n\n**Measured:** `_compute_membership` only records `dropped[netuid]` when `validity == \"negative\"` and `_eligible_for_removal(...)` is true; otherwise the netuid stays in `validity_map` and remains in `netuids` (`internal/subnet_universe.py`). **Inferred:** chain-negative netuids that have satisfied the existing 48h grace (`STALE_GRACE_SECONDS`) never move into `dropped` and never leave membership on this head.\n\n**Measured:** `_shrink_allowed` also requires `_eligible_for_removal` for each netuid in `prior − build` (`refresh_once` path). **Inferred:** even if a future build omitted netuids, shrink would stay blocked; with this bug the more common failure mode is **never shrinking** stale members because they never become removal-eligible in `_compute_membership`.\n\n## Severity\n\n| Finding | Severity | Label |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Literal `0` disables all removal eligibility | P0 | measured call + inferred behavior |\n| `DropEvidence` has no `token_count`; title mentions audit trails but nothing is wired | P1 | measured dataclass fields |\n| Stale netuids persist in membership / scoring denominator | P1 | inferred via `snapshot_coverage.load_membership_receipt` expectations |\n\n## Adversarial extremes\n\nExtreme inputs (`NaN`, `inf`, `1e308`) do not reach `_token_count_guard` because the argument is always `0` (**measured**). The failure mode is unconditional, not edge-case overflow.\n\n## Required fix direction\n\nPass the real audit-trail `token_count` (or add it to `DropEvidence` and thread from the writer) into `_token_count_guard`; add/adjust tests so a post-grace chain-negative netuid can still be dropped when `token_count > 0`, and cannot when `token_count == 0`. Do not ship with `_token_count_guard(0)`.\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | Traced `refresh_once` → `_compute_membership` → `_eligible_for_removal`; literal `0` blocks all drops | — |\n| owner-rules | 48h grace + chain-backed removal path effectively disabled; shrink safety semantics undermined | — |\n| settled-check | No settled doc in fixture repo for hard-coded `0`; treat as new defect | — |",
