            "body": "## Summary\n\nThe PR title describes capping **RPC batch size** with `max_tokens`, but the only behavioral change applies `_max_tokens_cap` to **`STALE_GRACE_SECONDS`** inside `_eligible_for_removal`. That helper is never used on probe/RPC batch paths in this diff.\n\n## Findings\n\n### P0 — Wrong value wired (`poisons-later-row`)\n\n**Measured:** At head, `STALE_GRACE_SECONDS = 172800` (48h). New code:\n\n```python\ndef _max_tokens_cap(batch: int, max_tokens: int = MAX_TOKENS) -> int:\n    return min(batch, max_tokens // 2)\n\nreturn (now - started).total_seconds() >= _max_tokens_cap(STALE_GRACE_SECONDS)\n```\n\n**Inferred:** With `MAX_TOKENS = 4096`, `_max_tokens_cap(172800) == min(172800, 2048) == 2048`. Negative netuids become eligible for removal after ~34 minutes instead of 48 hours.\n\n**Inferred:** `_eligible_for_removal` is on the real refresh entry path (`_compute_membership` → `_shrink_allowed` → `refresh_once` / `_publish`). Premature drops change persisted membership and every downstream reader (`get_netuids`, pump rows), so later cycles inherit the wrong universe — not a one-off crash.\n\n### P1 — Stated goal not implemented\n\n**Measured:** `_default_probe_fetch` still passes full `probe_candidates` lists to `get_member_netuids`; no `MAX_TOKENS` / `_max_tokens_cap` on batch size in this change.\n\n## Skills\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | Traced grace constant through `_max_tokens_cap` into removal eligibility on the worker refresh path | — |\n| owner-rules | Documented 48h grace in `_compute_membership` and `STALE_GRACE_SECONDS`; this diff silently replaces it with 2048s | — |\n| settled-check | 48h grace is an existing constant/decision; misusing a token batch helper on it is new, not settled | — |\n\n## Required fix\n\nUse `_max_tokens_cap` (or equivalent) where RPC **batch sizes** are chosen for chain reads; restore `_eligible_for_removal` to compare against `STALE_GRACE_SECONDS` unchanged. Add/adjust tests that assert grace remains 48h and batch caps match `max_tokens`.",
