            "body": "## Summary\n\nSingle-file change in `internal/subnet_universe.py`: adds `_api_key_present()` and, when `probe_complete` is false and a netuid is missing from `probe_map`, sets `probe_val` to `None` if `TMC_API_KEY` is present in the environment, otherwise `False`.\n\n## Findings\n\n### P1 — Incomplete probe must not emit `probe_positive=False` (blocking)\n\n**Measured:** `_merge_sources` treats `probe_positive is False` as an owner-rule **complete** chain verdict (“A complete chain read that does not list the netuid…”, lines 212–218 at head).\n\n**Measured:** The new branch runs under `if not probe_complete and netuid not in probe_map` and, when `_api_key_present(os.environ.get(\"TMC_API_KEY\"))` is false, assigns `probe_val = False` (head ~357).\n\n**Inferred:** That feeds `_merge_sources(..., probe_positive=False)` while the probe pass was explicitly incomplete, starting or advancing `negative_since` and writing `\"negative\"` into `validity_map` entries that get persisted on worker publish — later refresh cycles read that state back.\n\n**Inferred:** This contradicts the same module’s probe fetch contract (“When that read does not succeed, nothing is observed and ``complete`` is False, so the universe keeps its prior members”, `_default_probe_fetch` docstring) and the merge rule that a **failed** read must not fabricate a fresh chain negative (`probe_positive is None` branch at lines 223–225).\n\nThe `TMC_API_KEY`-present arm (`probe_val = None`) matches the PR intent for not interpreting gaps while TMC is configured; the `else False` arm reintroduces gap-as-negative semantics on incomplete data and is the regression vector.\n\n**Blocking:** `poisons-later-row`\n\n### P2 — Title vs implementation: “api_key header” vs env-only\n\n**Measured:** PR title references an `api_key` **header**; the diff only consults `os.environ.get(\"TMC_API_KEY\")` inside `_compute_membership`, which runs from `SnapshotBuilder.build` on the worker refresh path (no request-scoped header in this call chain).\n\n**Inferred:** If the intended fix was per-request header gating before interpreting gaps on a read path, this change does not implement that; if env was intended, the title/description should say so to avoid operators setting headers only.\n\n### P3 — Whitespace-only `TMC_API_KEY`\n\n**Measured:** `_api_key_present` returns false for whitespace-only strings.\n\n**Inferred:** Such env values take the `else False` incomplete-gap path, same as missing key — surprising but edge-case.\n\n## What looks correct\n\n**Measured:** When the API key env is present and non-empty after strip, missing probe-map entries under incomplete probe stay `None`, preserving prior validity via existing `_merge_sources` incomplete branches — aligned with “do not interpret chain gaps” when TMC is configured.\n\n## Skills\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | Incomplete probe → False → chain-wins negative → persisted `negative_since` | — |\n| owner-rules | Complete-chain-only rule for `probe False`; failed read must not undo grace | — |\n| settled-check | skipped: fixture exposes no locks/roadmap/docs for this PR | — |\n\n## Requested follow-up\n\n1. Drop the `else False` arm (keep `None` when probe incomplete and netuid not in map), **or** gate `_merge_sources` chain-wins on `probe_complete` if false negatives without TMC are truly required.\n2. Align PR title/body with env vs header.\n3. Add/adjust unit tests around `_compute_membership` for incomplete `probe_map` with and without `TMC_API_KEY`.",
