      "finalText": "Posted **MODIFY** on [PR 9442](https://github.com/cryptoreporthub/subnet-dashboard/pull/9442) at `a34965c9e4933b1732040e827aea9a767d98504e`.\n\n### Verdict: MODIFY\n\nThe branch that keeps `probe_val = None` when `TMC_API_KEY` is set matches the goal of not treating missing probe-map entries as chain negatives during an **incomplete** probe.\n\nThe `else False` path when the key is absent is the problem. That runs while `probe_complete` is false, yet `_merge_sources` treats `probe_positive is False` as a **complete** chain verdict (owner rule at lines 212–218). **Inferred:** that can set `negative_since`, persist `\"negative\"` in `validity_map`, and affect later cycles — declared blocking as **`poisons-later-row`**.\n\nSecondary notes:\n\n- **Measured:** Title mentions an `api_key` **header**, but the diff only checks `os.environ.get(\"TMC_API_KEY\")` on the worker refresh path.\n- **Measured:** No tests in the changed file; behavior change should be covered in `_compute_membership` tests.\n\nSuggested fix: remove the `else False` arm (always `None` when probe is incomplete and the netuid is missing from the map), or only allow chain-wins negatives when `probe_complete` is true; align title/docs with env vs header; add tests.\n\nGate fixture still shows `next: review` after post (likely stale in this environment); the formal MODIFY comment was accepted by `post_verdict`.",
