            "body": "## Summary\n\nPR extracts membership netuid ordering into `r1b_member_netuids_from_map_a` and calls it from `_compute_membership`. The helper is **not** equivalent to the line it replaces.\n\n## Findings\n\n### P1 — `if int(k)` drops root netuid 0 (behavior change)\n\n**Measured:** Base `_compute_membership` ends with:\n`netuids = sorted(int(k) for k in validity_map.keys())`.\n\n**Measured (diff):** Head helper returns:\n`sorted(int(k) for k in validity_map.keys() if int(k))`, which omits key `\"0\"` / `ROOT_NETUID`.\n\n**Measured:** `ROOT_NETUID = 0` with comment that membership adds root while chain probe skips it (`internal/subnet_universe.py`). `_compute_membership` adds `ROOT_NETUID` to candidates when `observed_members` is non-empty and can place `\"0\"` in `validity_map`.\n\n**Inferred:** After refresh, persisted snapshots can carry `validity_map[\"0\"]` while `netuids` and `_build_rows` output omit netuid 0. `/api/subnets` and pump rows no longer include root even when validity says it is a member.\n\n**Inferred:** `load_membership_receipt` exposes `root_netuid_in_membership: 0 in snap.netuids` (`internal/council/snapshot_coverage.py`); this becomes false whenever root remains in `validity_map` only — telemetry and operators lose the signal the code explicitly tracks.\n\n**Inferred:** If a prior LKG listed `0` in `netuids` and the new list omits `0` without an entry in `build.dropped` (root is never eligible for removal), `_shrink_allowed` returns false and refresh retains prior (`_hold_prior`) — membership updates stall while `validity_map` on the built snapshot still disagrees with published `netuids`.\n\nClassification: **poisons-later-row** (durable snapshot inconsistency and dependent readers).\n\n### P2 — Helper placement and import\n\n**Inferred:** Membership list logic in `internal/run_mode.py` (Fly/worker mode flags) is the wrong module boundary for universe membership; a function-local import inside `_compute_membership` adds per-refresh import cost.\n\n**Guess:** If the intent was a pure extract-refactor, the helper should match the old expression exactly (no truthiness filter) and live beside universe membership (or shared subnet helper), with a regression test for root-in-membership vs scoring exclusions.\n\n## What would unblock PASS\n\n1. Make `r1b_member_netuids_from_map_a` semantically identical to the removed one-liner **or** document and test an intentional root exclusion across persist, API rows, and `root_netuid_in_membership`.\n2. If root must stay out of `netuids`, remove or align `validity_map[\"0\"]` and update shrink/receipt logic in the same PR.\n3. Add/adjust tests covering refresh with root present in `validity_map` and prior LKG containing `0`.\n\nNo overflow / never-expires / crash-only edge cases found beyond existing `int(k)` parsing (unchanged).\n",
