            "body": "## Summary\n\nRefactor routes `_compute_membership` netuid list construction through `r1b_member_netuids_from_map_c` in `internal/council/score_cache.py`. The helper is not a straight lift of the old one-liner: it adds `if int(k)`, which drops netuid **0** from `netuids` even when `\"0\"` remains in `validity_map` (**measured**, diff + head file reads).\n\n## Findings\n\n### P2 — Implicit root exclusion + snapshot seam change (**inferred** product intent may match `ROOT_NETUID` comment, but diff does not prove it)\n\n**Base (882980b…):** `netuids = sorted(int(k) for k in validity_map.keys())` — any validity key, including `\"0\"`, becomes a member id.\n\n**Head:** `sorted(int(k) for k in validity_map.keys() if int(k))` — netuid 0 is omitted from `netuids` while `_compute_membership` can still write `validity_map[\"0\"]` when root is in `candidates` (**measured**).\n\nDownstream at head:\n- `_build_rows` iterates `netuids` only → no row for root when filtered (**inferred**).\n- `load_membership_receipt` exposes `root_netuid_in_membership: 0 in snap.netuids` (**measured** in `snapshot_coverage.py`) → flips when root was previously listed.\n- `membership_scoring_expected` already uses `int(n) > 0` (**measured**) — scoring denominator already ignored root; this change aligns **membership list** with that, but via truthiness on `int(k)` rather than an explicit rule.\n\n**Shrink / hold path (**inferred**):** If persisted `prior.netuids` contains `0` and a new build omits it without `dropped[0]` (root cannot be `_eligible_for_removal`), `_shrink_allowed` stays false and `_hold_prior` keeps the old list — root may linger in persisted `netuids` without a documented migration. Not an overflow/NaN path; not declared blocking.\n\n### P3 — Module placement and API clarity\n\nMembership derivation lives in `score_cache.py` (TTL scoring cache module) with an opaque name, no docstring, and no type hints (**measured**). Lazy import inside `_compute_membership` adds coupling from universe refresh to score cache (**inferred** import-cycle risk low from fixture read).\n\n### Adversarial extremes (read-only)\n\nNon-numeric `validity_map` keys still raise in `int(k)` on both base and head — can abort the membership compute (**measured**, same as before). No new `1e308`/TTL overflow surface in this diff.\n\n## Requested changes\n\n1. Document helper semantics (root excluded from member **list** vs keys in `validity_map`) and prefer explicit `int(k) > 0` or `k != str(ROOT_NETUID)` over `if int(k)`.\n2. Add or point to a test that pins netuid-0-in-map behavior for `_compute_membership` / receipt `root_netuid_in_membership`.\n3. Consider locating the helper next to universe or council membership code rather than `score_cache.py` unless R1b generalization strictly requires this module.\n\nNo blocking categories (`never-expires`, `overflow`, `aborts-cycle`, `poisons-later-row`) declared for PASS refusal.",
