            "body": "## Summary\n\nSingle-line change in `_compute_membership`: derive `netuids` from `validity_map` keys with `if int(k)`, excluding netuid `0` (`ROOT_NETUID`) from the published membership list while the loop can still retain a `\"0\"` validity entry when root is a candidate.\n\n## Trace (real entry: `SnapshotBuilder.build` → `_compute_membership` → `UniverseSnapshot` / `get_netuids` / pump rows)\n\n**Measured:** At base, `netuids = sorted(int(k) for k in validity_map.keys())` could include `0` when root stayed in `validity_map`. At head, `0` is omitted from `netuids`, so `_build_rows` and `get_netuids()` no longer surface a root row from this path.\n\n**Measured:** `ROOT_NETUID = 0` is documented as special (probe/membership semantics at module top). `_eligible_for_removal` already refuses removal of root. `_emergency_rows` skips `netuid == 0`.\n\n**Measured:** `internal/council/snapshot_coverage.load_membership_receipt` already filters `snap.netuids` with `int(n) > 0` and exposes `root_netuid_in_membership: 0 in snap.netuids`. Head behavior makes that telemetry false at the canonical snapshot source instead of only at receipt normalization.\n\n**Inferred:** If a persisted LKG still lists `0` in `prior.netuids`, dropping `0` without a `dropped[0]` entry makes `_shrink_allowed` fail (no eligible removal evidence) → `_hold_prior` retains LKG. No silent unsafe shrink.\n\n**Inferred:** Orphan `validity_map[\"0\"]` without `0` in `netuids` is slightly redundant in persisted JSON but does not change per-netuid grace/negative handling for tradable IDs.\n\n## Extremes\n\nNon-numeric validity keys: **unchanged** — `int(k)` was already required; bad keys still abort the membership build the same way (**inferred**, not executed).\n\nNo new float/NaN/inf paths in this diff.\n\n## Owner rules\n\nChain-wins negative merge and 48h grace logic are untouched. Excluding root from exported membership matches scoring admission docs (“Root (0) is never scored”) in `snapshot_coverage`.\n\n## Verdict rationale\n\nNo blocking never-expire, overflow, cycle-abort, or cross-row poison path identified. Optional follow-up (non-blocking): prefer `int(k) > 0` or `int(k) != ROOT_NETUID` over falsy `if int(k)` for readability — behavior equivalent for non-negative netuids.\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | Traced `_compute_membership` output through snapshot publish and receipt filtering; checked shrink gate when prior contained 0 | — |\n| owner-rules | Confirmed chain/grace paths unchanged; root exclusion aligns with scoring membership rules | — |\n| settled-check | Downstream receipt already filtered `>0`; change generalizes at helper source | — |",
