      "finalText": "**PASS** posted on [PR 9453](https://github.com/cryptoreporthub/subnet-dashboard/pull/9453) at `24f63b5611d21ac6c27ab662c8249a87f83363f6`.\n\nThe diff is one line in `_compute_membership`: `netuids` is built with `if int(k)`, so **netuid 0 is dropped from the published membership list** even when `\"0\"` can remain in `validity_map`.\n\n**Measured:** That matches existing intent elsewhere—`ROOT_NETUID` is special, emergency rows skip 0, and `snapshot_coverage.load_membership_receipt` already uses `int(n) > 0` and tracks `root_netuid_in_membership`. Centralizing the filter at the helper avoids exposing root via `get_netuids()` / `_build_rows`.\n\n**Measured:** If an old LKG still had `0` in `prior.netuids`, removing it without `dropped[0]` makes `_shrink_allowed` fail and **`_hold_prior` retains LKG**—no silent unsafe shrink.\n\n**Non-blocking note:** `if int(k)` is equivalent to `> 0` for normal netuids but reads obscurely; `!= ROOT_NETUID` or `> 0` would be clearer.\n\nNo blocking findings (`never-expires`, `overflow`, `aborts-cycle`, `poisons-later-row`). Gate fixture still shows `next: review`; Cursor/Ditto/suite steps follow the channel bot after MC verdict is recorded on the PR.",
