      "finalText": "**MODIFY** posted on [PR 9454](https://github.com/cryptoreporthub/subnet-dashboard/pull/9454) at head `ae2518217bd4ad0d957ff08f88cc0158efd62a6d`.\n\nThe change replaces inline `sorted(int(k) for k in validity_map.keys())` with `r1b_member_netuids_from_map_f`, which drops netuid **0** via `if int(k)`. That matches how scoring and chain membership already treat root, but it conflicts with **`_shrink_allowed`**: when LKG still lists `0`, the new build omits it without any `dropped[0]` entry (root can never be in `dropped` because `_eligible_for_removal` is false for `ROOT_NETUID`). Refresh then hits “unsafe shrink blocked” and **`_hold_prior`** keeps republishing the old snapshot, so root can stay in published membership across cycles. Blocking tag: **`poisons-later-row`**.\n\n**Ask before merge:** exempt `ROOT_NETUID` from the shrink-evidence check when it is the only removed netuid, or add an explicit LKG migration, plus a regression test for prior-with-0 → refresh.",
