            "body": "## Summary\n\nExtracts ISO parsing for `negative_since` into `_parse_negative_since` and calls it from `_eligible_for_removal`. Adds a small unit test (naive datetime → UTC, garbage → `None`).\n\n## Adversarial trace\n\n**Real entry path (inferred from head reads):** `SnapshotBuilder.build` → `_compute_membership` → `_eligible_for_removal(netuid, DropEvidence(...), now)` → parse `evidence.negative_since` → `(now - started).total_seconds() >= STALE_GRACE_SECONDS` (172800). `_shrink_allowed` uses the same helper for dropped netuids.\n\n**Measured (PR diff):** New helper is byte-for-byte equivalent to the former inline block: `str(value)`, `datetime.fromisoformat`, naive → `timezone.utc`, any failure → `None` → `_eligible_for_removal` returns `False`.\n\n**Measured (existing tests at head):** Grace removal is already exercised end-to-end (`test_negative_validity_removal_after_grace`, `test_chain_unregistered_tmc_listed_roresults: /tmp/r1-slot-ofIz.json
w_leaves_after_grace_and_stays_gone`, `test_shrink_allowed_*`, provider refresh tests, etc.). The new test only pins parser edge cases.\n\n## Extreme / failure modes\n\n| Input | Effect | Label |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Unparseable `negative_since` | Not removal-eligible; netuid stays in membership until a valid clock exists | **inferred** — unchanged from pre-refactor |\n| Naive ISO | Treated as UTC | **inferred** — unchanged; now explicitly tested |\n| `negative_since` from `_now_iso()` / persisted ISO | Normal grace math | **inferred** — `_merge_sources` still sets stamps via `_now_iso()`; this PR does not touch merge logic |\n| Future `started` | `total_seconds()` negative → below grace threshold → no early removal | **inferred** — unchanged |\n| `1e308` / non-ISO strings | Parse fails → same as garbage | **guess** — not a realistic persisted shape; same as before |\n\nNo path found where this refactor alone makes a grace-eligible negative **never** leave after 48h, overflows to `inf`/`NaN` in the comparison, aborts a refresh cycle, or poisons a later row’s state.\n\n## Owner rules\n\n**Measured:** Diff touches only parser extraction + test; `_merge_sources`, chain-wins comments, partial-read grace retention, and shrink guards are untouched.\n\n## Note on tooling\n\n**Measured:** `get_pr_diff` shows the extracted helper; one `read_repo_file` slice at the same head SHA still showed inline parsing (fixture inconsistency). Verdict is based on the diff plus surrounding head context and tests, including the new `test_parse_negative_since_treats_naive_as_utc` present at head.\n\n## Verdict\n\nBehavior-neutral refactor with useful parser coverage. **PASS.**",
