cing ints.\n\n**P3 — No upper bound.** **Inferred:** absurd `MAX_TOKENS` could stress LLM/API batch paths once wired; not a parser bug by itself.\n\n**P3 — Naming/placement.** Batch sizing lives under `r1b_redact_clean_tokens.py` while the PR describes council batches; organizational only.\n\nNo blocking gate classes: no evidence in this diff of never-expiring rows, float overflow in-path, cycle abort from uncaught parse, or poisoned cross-row state.\n\n## Recommendation\n\nExtend tests for env override, invalid values, and floor clamp; align with existing `env_int` (reuse, move shared helper, or document intentional fail-soft vs fail-loud). Wire or follow-up PR should cap or validate against provider limits when integrated.",
